{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev","id":790883,"title":"Slashers & Ashwood Abbey Open Dev","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-22T09:15:57-08:00","id":790883,"title":"Slashers & Ashwood Abbey Open Dev","content":"find it <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/hunter-2e-open-dev-slashers-and-ashwood-abbey/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>!<br /> <br /> Discuss!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:13:14-08:00","id":790904,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Which of these three options do you prefer and why?<ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Option 3. Neither I nor my players have ever seen the Ashwood Abbey as anything but full-on antagonists. Even the one or two players I have that have expressed an interest in playing an Ashwood Abbey Hunter have stated they actively wish to play the role of the antagonist in the story. Therefore, I would vastly prefer to see a non-American and non-European Hunter group to add more variety to HtV.</span></li> </ul></li> <li>If you\u2019re worried about a change, what is your hangup and how do you feel this\u2019ll affect your group?<ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My only concern is that the Ashwood Abbey's rape-torture-murder shtick might be &quot;glorified&quot; in some way. I don't consider this likely, but it's still a concern.</span></li> </ul></li> <li>If you\u2019re excited by a specific idea, what do you like most about it?<ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'm excited about the possible replacement for the Ashwood Abbey, perhaps a Latin-American Hunter group, or even an African one. Definitely hoping it's something as diametrically different from the Ashwood Abbey as possible.</span></li> </ul></li> <li>If you already play Hunter, are Tier Two chronicles your preferred style of gameplay?<ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sorta. I don't really follow the Tier conventions. I downscale the Tier 3 Conspiracies to something more resembling the reach and power of a Tier 2 Compact, and then keep my Hunter games somewhere between Tier 1 and Tier 2. So the answer would be &quot;yes, sorta.&quot;</span></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:24:40-08:00","id":790911,"title":"","content":"Have already responded in the thread itself but felt like popping in here. I really like the Abbey, I always have. There's been something incredibly human about them, insofar as humans are bastards and will generally look for an excuse to exploit whatever they come across. There's also a lot more depth and potential there for being more than thrill-kill crazies. Hell, even their Compact splat has examples of guys who get dragged in unawares.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'm not the only player who'd miss them if they were to be thrown on the fire. I personally backed option two, since I think that the Abbey as a potentially sinking ship offers up lots of different ways to play with it- which could even include the 3rd scenario, if things go too badly. Something that would allow the Hunt Club to press their luck and gain a nice meaty place in the Slasher Chronicle, but also lay out the potential for reform, redemption or ruin within the Abbey itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:25:02-08:00","id":790913,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Abbey as antagonists. I like the idea of a new Compact from another part of the world. I hate the idea of taking what was a morally ambiguous faction in 1e and placing them firmly in the &quot;bad guy&quot; camp. I'd rather see them be treated like Seeers of the Throne in Mage 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:35:09-08:00","id":790915,"title":"","content":"as I said in the blog, I really like the Ashwood Abbey, and I don't have a problem with them being hedonistic, self serving monster killers who allow themselves to ignore some red lines as long as the target is a monster. Marking them as &quot;corrupted and evil group&quot; just because they do some ugly things doesn't make them into slashers, and it would really harm the moral ambiguity of Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:52:58-08:00","id":790922,"title":"","content":"I genuinely don't understand the problem that people have with their favourite group becoming antagonistic. I understand it if it was being changed in some major way, but it was to my understanding that players can be members of antagonistic groups easily? Or was that just me? Because usually antagonist groups have pages and pages of fluff, mechanics and backstory that seemed to indicate &quot;this is for players too.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T10:54:57-08:00","id":790925,"title":"","content":"Because it is not about turning them into antagonists- it is about turning them into slashers, being taken over by the Hunt Club, and while I allow many things in my table, playing a slasher is something I really feel uncomfortable with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:14:01-08:00","id":790933,"title":"","content":"I actually find that the Ashwood Abbey's current rape-torture theme is by far entire degrees worse than simple murder, and I would be more comfortable with a player who wants to play a full-on Slasher instead of an Ashwood Abbey Hunter, but I do understand that it's probably one of those very personal things that is bound to elicit very different opinions from people.<br /> <br /> So now that I understand that people are more concerned with the Ashwood Abbey being lumped with the slasher group, I definitely sympathise with where the AA fans are coming from. That said, I don't think the intent is to turn them <i>all</i> into Slashers. I think from the write-up, the idea is simply that there are <i>more</i> Slashers (since AA already had them in the first place).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:24:04-08:00","id":790937,"title":"","content":"I think that the implication is that there are more Slashers regardless of the choice; that comes across as purely a background theme to the Chronicle. Option 3 is explicit in that the Hunt Club subsumes the Abbey. Sure, they probably wouldn't all be Slashers, but the Slashers of the Hunt Club would have usurped the Abbey and begun to infect it with their ideas and methodologies- totally, utterly and completely. So you're either a Slasher or as good as a Slasher. If that's the case then Option 2 is the more nuanced approach because it shows us that fall happening. I'd rather be involved in the battle for the Abbey's soul than in the aftermath knowing that we've lose, and truly lost the way.<br /> <br /> It also feels a little opportunistic to be leveraging the death of the Abbey against getting a new Compact, especially one that promises to be more diverse; but that's another issue entirely.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think with the Abbey there's always a line in the sand, and though it'll vary from Cell to Cell, it's still there. There's a restraining bolt that keeps them human and keeps them from doing things to other humans (look how quickly they turned on Saucy Jack), but Slashers don't have that. They're a truly evil construct, no matter their origins. They can't be understood or reasoned with, and they'll never have the chance to be turned by a conscience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 12-22-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:49:36-08:00","id":790951,"title":"","content":"I really don't like the idea of Ashwood Abbey as antagonists. Every compact and every conspiracy can take the place of antagonists in games, in fact their stereotypes usually play up this angle.<br /> <br /> A question for the fans.<br /> <br /> A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:53:14-08:00","id":790954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the idea of Ashwood Abbey as antagonists. Every compact and every conspiracy can take the place of antagonists in games, in fact their stereotypes usually play up this angle.<br /> <br /> A question for the fans.<br /> <br /> A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, really, only The Union could be said to be the &quot;good guys&quot; of the core Hunter splats, given that they're the ones without a real agenda beyond &quot;Help the people who need helping.&quot; There are one or two other examples in the supplements that fit as well, though again they have their own motivations and drives. I never really saw Hunter as &quot;The Good guys&quot;, so much as people making the best (or taking advantage, more often) of a terrible situation. You don't have to be a good person to take up the candle, more often than not you just have to be driven or desperate enough.<br /> <br /> Even then, now that I think about it The Union also have the guys who go after street thugs and wife beaters and the like; so even they have moral foibles and push the limits of the Vigil away from the deserving,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 12-22-2015, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T11:58:03-08:00","id":790963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's usually how I play Hunter, since I enjoy variety in my games. For playing up the idea of empowered mortals of ambiguous morality, there's always Mage. For playing up the idea of a monster who may become as terrible as those he hunts, there's Werewolf (and Changeling, if you run a True-Fae-focused game), and even the new Beast, from what I heard in other threads. For playing up the idea of a dark hunter/predator, there's Vampire (and Beast). If you want vanilla mortals confronting the supernatural, there's the corebook mortals (perhaps with supernatural merits).<br /> <br /> I enjoy the idea of a game that brings a different playing experience from other games, so that no matter what kind of character or theme the player/ST wants to explore, there's always a gameline best suited for them.<br /> <br /> So in general my Hunters tend to be people who mean well. Of course, that doesn't mean they don't make mistakes, or have prejudices, or get carried away, or have secrets and vices that others can exploit, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:07:57-08:00","id":790974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790915#post790915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as I said in the blog, I really like the Ashwood Abbey, and I don't have a problem with them being hedonistic, self serving monster killers who allow themselves to ignore some red lines as long as the target is a monster. Marking them as &quot;corrupted and evil group&quot; just because they do some ugly things doesn't make them into slashers, and it would really harm the moral ambiguity of Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Stated perfectly.<br /> <br /> Really hope option 3 is not chosen as it would GREATLY reduce my excitement for Hunter 2.<br /> <br /> And this is only, like, the second dev blog? Sheesh!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:12:11-08:00","id":790980,"title":"","content":"My problem with the Ashwood Abbey is that I can't find any redeeming features with the organisation. Could anyone who likes them please post any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:20:06-08:00","id":790986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790980#post790980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Ashwood Abbey is that I can't find any redeeming features with the organisation. Could anyone who likes them please post any?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have fun. They don't worry about the moral issues, monsters are monsters to them. They're good at what they do, and do it proudly. They celebrate their victories, guaranteeing that after your death you won't be buried in a shallow grave and forgotten. They often have contacts in powerful places. They're often willing to help other hunters, and members have access to a wide support network.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-22-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:24:12-08:00","id":790991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's missing a bit of where a lot of people (including myself) come from.<br /> <br /> I want all of the PC groups to be plausible as seeing themselves as the good guys <i>in-character</i>, even if I find their methods morally dubious, to outright evil.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Abbey, is that it's really hard to imagine them as actually buying that they're doing anything &quot;good&quot; for anyone. I think this is where most of the Abbey's detractors are coming from. The Abbey does nothing for &quot;moral ambiguity&quot; because they're overtly amoral at best. They don't believe they're serving the greater good. They're not even inherently serving the greater good incidentally. <br /> <br /> Some people have expressed liking the idea of &quot;fighting for the soul of the Abbey,&quot; but that's only interesting if you think the Abbey has a soul, instead of having long since hunted it down, and gang-raped it to death.<br /> <br /> The Abbey, as-is, is already past the useful point of being good for the moral grey areas of Hunter. They're bad people, that do bad things, and are Hunter by sole virtue of their targets being monsters (some of whom are probably not as bad as the Abbey itself anyway). They've already fallen off the&quot;evil&quot; side of things enough that they stopped doing anything for playing with morally questionable Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:25:20-08:00","id":790992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>well... its complicated.<br /> <br /> Sure, some hunters are good guys- and there is nothing wrong with using them as good guys!- but all in all, Hunter is so much more than that. I mean, the splat which tries the best to be &quot;good guys&quot; in Hunter are the Lucifuge- and they are the children of the devil. Being an hunter doesn't require you some sort of moral superiority, or even thinking you have one. It only means you bump into the wrong thing at night, survive it and instead of deny what happened, being manipulated by it or turning fascinated, you decide to go and hunt it down. Being a good guy might help you maintain your sanity, but it doesn't what carrying the Vigil means, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:28:05-08:00","id":790993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790986#post790986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really a redeeming feature for an organization that hunts and kills thinking and feeling creatures.<br /> <br /> &quot;We care more about how fun a target will be to hunt, than any actual threat it poses to humanity&quot; is part of why people don't find them redeeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:28:07-08:00","id":790994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790991#post790991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's missing a bit of where a lot of people (including myself) come from.<br /> <br /> I want all of the PC groups to be plausible as seeing themselves as the good guys <i>in-character</i>, even if I find their methods morally dubious, to outright evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that fall under 'they're supposed to be the good guys,' with the caveat that they just think they are?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:28:38-08:00","id":790995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790991#post790991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's missing a bit of where a lot of people (including myself) come from.<br /> <br /> I want all of the PC groups to be plausible as seeing themselves as the good guys <i>in-character</i>, even if I find their methods morally dubious, to outright evil.<br /> <br /> The problem with the Abbey, is that it's really hard to imagine them as actually buying that they're doing anything &quot;good&quot; for anyone. I think this is where most of the Abbey's detractors are coming from. The Abbey does nothing for &quot;moral ambiguity&quot; because they're overtly amoral at best. They don't believe they're serving the greater good. They're not even inherently serving the greater good incidentally.<br /> <br /> Some people have expressed liking the idea of &quot;fighting for the soul of the Abbey,&quot; but that's only interesting if you think the Abbey has a soul, instead of having long since hunted it down, and gang-raped it to death.<br /> <br /> The Abbey, as-is, is already past the useful point of being good for the moral grey areas of Hunter. They're bad people, that do bad things, and are Hunter by sole virtue of their targets being monsters (some of whom are probably not as bad as the Abbey itself anyway). They've already fallen off the&quot;evil&quot; side of things enough that they stopped doing anything for playing with morally questionable Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they can, and do, recognise that they're doing a public service. That's what seperates them from the Hunt Club, that's what made them kill Jack when he went back to prostitutes. The Abbey has its own tattered sense of morality. It hunts down the things that hunt humanity, and they enjoy doing it- they take their fill. They use every part of the buffalo, as it were.<br /> <br /> Just as other Hunter groups have their examples of nuance and balance, so too will the Abbey- from the reluctant inductees to the ones who actually see a bit of purpose. I think it's reductive to basically say that there's no hope for the Abbey and that the organisation has no soul (properly or narratively) when they've often positioned themselves between the darkness and humanity (and indeed, between themselves and humanity.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790993#post790993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really a redeeming feature for an organization that hunts and kills thinking and feeling creatures.<br /> <br /> &quot;We care more about how fun a target will be to hunt, than any actual threat it poses to humanity&quot; is part of why people don't find them redeeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Hunters kill thinking and feeling creatures. Hell, even the Bear Lodge do it as a test of skill. They hunt things that are also a threat to humanity; two birds, one stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:30:45-08:00","id":790996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790994#post790994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't that fall under 'they're supposed to be the good guys,' with the caveat that they just think they are?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't see that there's a significant thematic difference between, &quot;you're playing the good guys,&quot; and, &quot;you're playing people that think they're the good guys, but maybe they should question that more...&quot; I'm not sure I can really help explain it further.<br /> <br /> So, no, it doesn't fall under, &quot;they're supposed to be the good guys.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:35:38-08:00","id":790998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the idea of Ashwood Abbey as antagonists. Every compact and every conspiracy can take the place of antagonists in games, in fact their stereotypes usually play up this angle.<br /> <br /> A question for the fans.<br /> <br /> A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually run Hunter as the villains. Chronicles of Darkness is a very grey vs. grey setting, where there are no clear good guys, everyone is just different shades of bad. But at my table, Hunters are the exception. They're the &quot;good guys&quot; in a setting where everyone else is the &quot;bad guys&quot; which makes them the de facto antagonists.<br /> <br /> I like Hunters to <i>look</i> genuinely altruistic from a human-centric perspective; the lights in the darkness, driving back the forces of evil for the sake of all mankind. But in the Chronicles of Darkness, that unquestioned sense of righteousness is exactly what makes them the worst of the worst. At least the monsters are self-aware enough to know when they're doing wrong (wether or not they care varies from one individual to the next). But Hunters don't even consider that maybe they're not so morally unimpeachable as they think. It's like when a victim of bullying becomes a bully - you'll never convince them they're anything but a victim fighting back.<br /> <br /> What I hope the Slasher Chronicle does is emphasizes that Hunters are just one little push away from being Slashers. Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club are a great example of just how similar Hunters and Slashers can be, and that's why I think it would be a shame to consolidate them. It takes a great moral quandary of &quot;what really separates the Abbey from the Hunt Club?&quot; and answers it with a predictable and boring &quot;nothing at all.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:38:31-08:00","id":790999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790980#post790980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with the Ashwood Abbey is that I can't find any redeeming features with the organisation. Could anyone who likes them please post any?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are bastards. I mean it, they are people who allow themselves to do the worst things they can ever imagine just because their enemy is not &quot;like them&quot;. They are degenerate crazies who enjoy life to the fullest, a ship of fools who parties every night with everything that money can buy. Each day is celebration, each hunt is a festival. Life is too sort to waste them on searching for some &quot;higher meaning&quot; about their hunt- and they are honest, brutally, brutally honest. Other hunters try to justify their acts for some higher cause, but they don't. They say the truth- they hunt monsters because it is fun. You can try and say you do it for god, or for justice, or for ages old feud, but eventually you hunt because it makes you feel alive, and all bellow those righteous words and fancy justifications, you are just like them- blood soaked and smiling like a madman. Sure, some of them may fall too far, but for they hunt them too. They are the humanity at its worst- and they still manage to light a candle to light their way in the night.<br /> <br /> So if you ask about how the Abbey contribute to Hunter's moral ambiguity as whole, it is by showing you just how far you can fall before you can no longer be considered as an hunter. Any more than that, and you are a monster. In sort, the discussion is not &quot;just&quot; about where the Abbey should be in the book, but how one defines what it means to be an hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:39:13-08:00","id":791000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790993#post790993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really a redeeming feature for an organization that hunts and kills thinking and feeling creatures.<br /> <br /> &quot;We care more about how fun a target will be to hunt, than any actual threat it poses to humanity&quot; is part of why people don't find them redeeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Agreed. I don't like thrill-killers. And I most certainly don't find it a redeeming quality to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:42:26-08:00","id":791005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790995#post790995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they can, and do, recognise that they're doing a public service.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really the organization's driving principle. They don't hunt monsters as a public service, and just happen to enjoy it. They hunt monsters for fun, or members for breaking their rules, and if it happens to end up being a public service that time, it's a bit of icing on the cake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what seperates them from the Hunt Club, that's what made them kill Jack when he went back to prostitutes. The Abbey has its own tattered sense of morality. It hunts down the things that hunt humanity, and they enjoy doing it- they take their fill. They use every part of the buffalo, as it were. </div> </div> </div>If that's all that separates them, the line is insignificant. I can make a great case for why Adolf Hitler was an order of magnitude or two more evil than Saddam Husein, but that doesn't stop Saddam from being an irredeemable sociopath in the eyes of history.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Abbey could be worse,&quot; doesn't demonstrate that they're already on the wrong side of the line of, &quot;So bad it doesn't matter.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just as other Hunter groups have their examples of nuance and balance, so too will the Abbey-... </div> </div> </div>&quot;Will&quot; I think is the core issue here. The Abbey as-is isn't good for HtV. Whether you want to redo them into something that's better for nuance and balance, or scrap them, let them be antagonists, and have something else take their place is irrelevant to the problems with how they <i>are</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Hunters kill thinking and feeling creatures. Hell, even the Bear Lodge do it as a test of skill. They hunt things that are also a threat to humanity; two birds, one stone. </div> </div> </div>And this is completely missing the point I made. I'm having trouble seeing it as anything put purposefully so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:43:42-08:00","id":791007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791000#post791000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Agreed. I don't like thrill-killers. And I most certainly don't find it a redeeming quality to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it though that it's only with the Abbey that people start to get misty eyed with the concept of killing monsters? Is the Null Mysteris guy who's dissecting a werewolf to see how it ticks really any better than one of the Abbey who wants an adrenaline rush? Are -any- of the Bear Lodge? Are the Cainites any more justified in their ostentatious and bloody murders?<br /> <br /> If we're talking moral victories, then the only ones you really root for are VASCU- because they'll only kill if forced to. Everyone else is just as bloody-handed and just as guilty as the Abbey. Their only real crime is that they have the audacity to enjoy what they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791005#post791005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is completely missing the point I made. I'm having trouble seeing it as anything put purposefully so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely not meaning to; just pointing out, as above, that it only seems to become a problem when the Abbey do it. Literally every Hunter group is killing living things with untold depths and dreams of their own, and that entirely doesn't matter because of what those things are and what they do. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 12-22-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:50:37-08:00","id":791011,"title":"","content":"Personally, what I'd do to the Ashwood Abbey to preserve their &quot;theme&quot; and moral ambiguity but make them a lot more palatable, would be to go in one of two directions:<br /> <br /> A) The Ashwood Abbey tortures, yes, but they do it for a reason. No other Hunter group has more intimate information on the nature of the things that lurk in the dark than the Ashwood Abbey. They torture secrets out of monsters and keep a library of bloody confessions. They're rich, of course, even if they members weren't, they'd make several fortunes selling off their occult secrets. However, this version of the Ashwood Abbey does not do its grisly work for fun. It does it for a purpose, and that purpose is extracting as much knowledge as they can get from a monster before the body or the mind give way.<br /> <br /> B) The Ashwood Abbey hunts and kills monsters for fun, sure, but they don't torture. They are above such bloody, plebeian practices. Instead, this version of the Ashwood Abbey focuses more on the game of status, politics and accomplishments, rather than on the decadence. They're bored aristocrats on a world-spanning safari.<br /> <br /> Note that in both these cases, the sexual element of the Ashwood Abbey has been completely abandoned. This is absolutely crucial. I don't think I or any of my players could stomach a group that enacts sexual violence on anyone (even monsters) and isn't an antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:51:08-08:00","id":791012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790999#post790999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are bastards. I mean it, they are people who allow themselves to do the worst things they can ever imagine just because their enemy is not &quot;like them&quot;. They are degenerate crazies who enjoy life to the fullest, a ship of fools who parties every night with everything that money can buy. Each day is celebration, each hunt is a festival. Life is too sort to waste them on searching for some &quot;higher meaning&quot; about their hunt- and they are honest, brutally, brutally honest. Other hunters try to justify their acts for some higher cause, but they don't. They say the truth- they hunt monsters because it is fun. You can try and say you do it for god, or for justice, or for ages old feud, but eventually you hunt because it makes you feel alive, and all bellow those righteous words and fancy justifications, you are just like them- blood soaked and smiling like a madman. Sure, some of them may fall too far, but for they hunt them too. They are the humanity at its worst- and they still manage to light a candle to light their way in the night.<br /> <br /> So if you ask about how the Abbey contribute to Hunter's moral ambiguity as whole, it is by showing you just how far you can fall before you can no longer be considered as an hunter. Any more than that, and you are a monster. In sort, the discussion is not &quot;just&quot; about where the Abbey should be in the book, but how one defines what it means to be an hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This expresses what I like about Ashwood Abbey more eloquently than I think I ever could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791000#post791000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Agreed. I don't like thrill-killers. And I most certainly don't find it a redeeming quality to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their redeeming quality is that they are <i>honest</i>. They don't try to justify the hunt as a moral imperitive, they admit to themselves and to others that they like to harm and kill intelligent, thinking beings because it's fun, and as long as they're not doing it to humans no one will mind. They're like the Dexters of ChroD. I don't think anyone would deny that Dexter is a horrible person, and so are the Abbey horrible people. But frankly, I think most Hunters are, the Abbey just admits it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-22-2015, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:55:18-08:00","id":791014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791007#post791007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is it though that it's only with the Abbey that people start to get misty eyed with the concept of killing monsters? Is the Null Mysteris guy who's dissecting a werewolf to see how it ticks really any better than one of the Abbey who wants an adrenaline rush? Are -any- of the Bear Lodge? Are the Cainites any more justified in their ostentatious and bloody murders?<br /> <br /> If we're talking moral victories, then the only ones you really root for are VASCU- because they'll only kill if forced to. Everyone else is just as bloody-handed and just as guilty as the Abbey. Their only real crime is that they have the audacity to enjoy what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point. Killing people fun is despicable, WoD is pretty big on the &quot;people are monsters, monsters are people&quot;-theme. Anyhow the Bear Lodge is just as bad as the Abbey.<br /> The Cainites are doing their hunts out of insane religious obligation. Still bad, but at least they have a REASON. The Les Mysteres are also utterly wrong, but they too have a reason beyond &quot;I'm bored, let's kill and/or fuck monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Cheiron Group are probably tied with the Abbey with most villainous, but at least the ground level people can be decent there. Just regular people who didn't realize what they signed up for, and are now stuck working for an evil company, or else, and other reasons like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:57:08-08:00","id":791018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why a lot of people seem to come at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys is pretty simple: when you get down it, Hunter is the game of &quot;there are things that go bump in the night; it's your calling to bump back&quot;. The whole idea of the game is that you're a human who has the audacity to try and fight back against the creatures that lurk in the darkness - there's a very big &quot;Mortal Empowerment&quot; theme to Hunter.<br /> <br /> Now, the game doesn't directly state this, but it's a theme that's readily seized upon by the &quot;Humanity, Fuck Yeah!&quot; fandom. Fighting monsters automatically makes you the Good Guy, it's just how people tend to think.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, the majority opinion generally would be that Hunters are the Good Guy faction. Because they go out and oppose monsters. There's a reason that the least popular groups are generally either the cancerous ones (Les Mysteres and Knights of St. George as prime examples) or the villainous ones (Ashwood Abbey being the best example); these stand counter to the general assumption players have going in that &quot;we're humans, they're monsters, we're supposed to be the Good Guys - we may risk losing ourselves in the fights, but we're still the Right Side going in&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> On topic, I'm personally fine with whatever happens to Ashwood Abbey. It's always been Token Evil Teammate of the corebook's compacts, so as far as I'm concerned, it can't get much worse. The whole idea of it is that it's a Hellfire Club that's clued into the fact that there really are monsters out there. There's not much you can really do with that without leaving them heavily towards the Black side of the Black &amp; Gray Morality scale. At best they're hedonistic thrill-killers who regard monsters as the ultimate thrill, or a cancer compact that happily interacts with monsters who can provide thrills (the two options not being mutually exclusive).<br /> <br /> Really, the only way I've ever been able to keep the Abbey and the Club seperate in my head is by remembering that the Abbey at least has the guts to go after monsters that can really fight back. The Club just picks on ordinary humans, and usually ends up coming off the worst when it does bump into supernatural creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","user":"VoidDrifter","date":". 12-23-2015, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T12:59:09-08:00","id":791023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791011#post791011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that in both these cases, the sexual element of the Ashwood Abbey has been completely abandoned. This is absolutely crucial. I don't think I or any of my players could stomach a group that enacts sexual violence on anyone (even monsters) and isn't an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this I could totally get behind. Maybe shift that aspect over to the Hunt Club, and make it one of the reasons an Abbey member might turn Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:00:16-08:00","id":791024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791014#post791014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the point. Killing people fun is despicable, WoD is pretty big on the &quot;people are monsters, monsters are people&quot;-theme. Anyhow the Bear Lodge is just as bad as the Abbey.<br /> The Cainites are doing their hunts out of insane religious obligation. Still bad, but at least they have a REASON. The Les Mysteres are also utterly wrong, but they too have a reason beyond &quot;I'm bored, let's kill and/or fuck monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Cheiron Group are probably tied with the Abbey with most villainous, but at least the ground level people can be decent there. Just regular people who didn't realize what they signed up for, and are now stuck working for an evil company, or else, and other reasons like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they were killing people that would be an issue, but they're not. They're killing monsters, the same as every other Hunter. We all know from the other gamelines that every single supernatural group has its own nuances and agendas and that they're not all truly evil- and occasionally that will wrong foot a Hunter- but they are monsters. Killing them for fun is just as valid as killing them out of one of the many misguided religious agendas. As has been expressed elsewhere, there's an honesty to the Abbey. They're killing to indulge themselves while removing something that shouldn't be. There's one of the &quot;working with&quot; blurbs where someone watches them poison a witch and then leave, happy as can be. This allows me to ask, gleefully and in all honesty, is it really more evil to kill evil at dinner than for VALKYRIE to burn them in battle? (Sorry; couldn't resist a good Tywin-ing)<br /> <br /> The difference between the Abbey and other Hunters are ultimately little more than self-justifying semantics. The thrill of the hunt is just as valid an interpretation as fighting for decades old guilt or scientific curiosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 12-22-2015, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:06:58-08:00","id":791029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790974#post790974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is only, like, the second dev blog? Sheesh!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is almost as if the Developer wants to hear from people playing Hunter and get their thoughts on some complex parts of the game...<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:15:44-08:00","id":791033,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be interesting to see the Abbey become the compact that's most likely to make friends with certain factions of monsters and then hunt down other monsters (possibly of the same type).<br /> <br /> Keep the murder and the fucking, but make it murder AND fucking, not murder-fucking.<br /> <br /> They're rich, bored, and well connected, they in many ways make the perfect hit-men for Supernaturals looking to off another Supernatural.<br /> <br /> Sure, maybe you have to &quot;degrade&quot; yourself a little and fuck a bunch of humans while in <i>Urshul</i>, but it might be fun, too; and when you attack that Pure tribe just outside of the city they'll already be dealing with a bunch of thrill seeking yahoos making the hunt all the easier. And if they happen to capture one of the Pure, stick them on a stick, and serve them up at the next shindig? Well, not your lookout, fucker should have thought about that before turning their back on Luna.<br /> <br /> Basically I think that the Abbey should be the Hunter group with the inside track when it comes to getting information from other Supernaturals. And the cool parties that everyone, even the Prince, would like to receive an invite to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:17:40-08:00","id":791034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791033#post791033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'd be interesting to see the Abbey become the compact that's most likely to make friends with certain factions of monsters and then hunt down other monsters (possibly of the same type).<br /> <br /> Keep the murder and the fucking, but make it murder AND fucking, not murder-fucking.<br /> <br /> They're rich, bored, and well connected, they in many ways make the perfect hit-men for Supernaturals looking to off another Supernatural.<br /> <br /> Sure, maybe you have to &quot;degrade&quot; yourself a little and fuck a bunch of humans while in <i>Urshul</i>, but it might be fun, too; and when you attack that Pure tribe just outside of the city they'll already be dealing with a bunch of thrill seeking yahoos making the hunt all the easier. And if they happen to capture one of the Pure, stick them on a stick, and serve them up at the next shindig? Well, not your lookout, fucker should have thought about that before turning their back on Luna.<br /> <br /> Basically I think that the Abbey should be the Hunter group with the inside track when it comes to getting information from other Supernaturals. And the cool parties that everyone, even the Prince, would like to receive an invite to.</div> </div> </div> </div>See now that's nice, and probably how a lot of Cancer Cells justify things to themselves, to boot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:26:31-08:00","id":791044,"title":"","content":"If I had to vote for one of the three options presented I'd go for No Change. However my true preference would be to really examine what &quot;hedonistic thrill seeker with no morals&quot; actually means and refocus the Abbey in that direction.<br /> <br /> Lets put it this way. You have wealth, power, no morals, and all the supernatural before you. Is torturing someone really the most fun activity you can think of?<br /> <br /> It seems to me that if the Abby were really about thrills, they'd be more interested in finding some Witch (preferably non-Supernal and so no Disbelief) who could give them the power to fly than a Witch to torture. Of course since they have no morals they'd be willing to torture said Witch if he wasn't willing to do the magic for simple cash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790915#post790915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as I said in the blog, I really like the Ashwood Abbey, and I don't have a problem with them being hedonistic, self serving monster killers who allow themselves to ignore some red lines as long as the target is a monster. Marking them as &quot;corrupted and evil group&quot; just because they do some ugly things doesn't make them into slashers, and it would really harm the moral ambiguity of Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T13:55:04-08:00","id":791070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790999#post790999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They are bastards. I mean it, they are people who allow themselves to do the worst things they can ever imagine just because their enemy is not &quot;like them&quot;. They are degenerate crazies who enjoy life to the fullest, a ship of fools who parties every night with everything that money can buy. Each day is celebration, each hunt is a festival. Life is too sort to waste them on searching for some &quot;higher meaning&quot; about their hunt- and they are honest, brutally, brutally honest. Other hunters try to justify their acts for some higher cause, but they don't. They say the truth- they hunt monsters because it is fun. You can try and say you do it for god, or for justice, or for ages old feud, but eventually you hunt because it makes you feel alive, and all bellow those righteous words and fancy justifications, you are just like them- blood soaked and smiling like a madman. Sure, some of them may fall too far, but for they hunt them too. They are the humanity at its worst- and they still manage to light a candle to light their way in the night.<br /> <br /> So if you ask about how the Abbey contribute to Hunter's moral ambiguity as whole, it is by showing you just how far you can fall before you can no longer be considered as an hunter. Any more than that, and you are a monster. In sort, the discussion is not &quot;just&quot; about where the Abbey should be in the book, but how one defines what it means to be an hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellently put.<br /> <br /> The Abbey has always appeared to me as more than just the token evil group, but rather the most human and personal compact. Sure the part of humanity they demonstrate is often the worst and most morally vile, but that is only if you use the group as it is seen on its surface. Under it all the Abbey can be used to house hunters who are in it for their own reason and not for any ideaology or responsibility.<br /> <br /> With Hunter 2e coming out and the question of what to do with them and the Club, I find it out odd that the Club is so easily considered just a compact for Slashers. What I mean by this is that as they are portrayed they are a very specific group of Killers that would not readily include all Slashers (Masks, etc.). With that it never occured to me to make them all Slashers because it almost assumes that any human murderer is a Slasher. I think a useful way to use the CoD rules and concepts to integrate the two groups is perhaps to set up the Club as a cult with a Slasher at the top. This cult then poaches members from the Abbey when they can and hunts the others. This conflict could be idealogically shown in how the Abbey sees itself as libertine while the Club believes and follows its hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T14:00:19-08:00","id":791071,"title":"","content":"Some further thoughts.<br /> <br /> Slashers don't actually fit the Abbey that well. A Slasher is defined by compulsion, and being a creature of very strict habits. Look at the Legend Undertaking for the most obvious example, or <i>VASCU Case study : \u201cNone\u201d</i>. The Abbey strike me as the exact opposite, always on a quest for novelty.<br /> <br /> A Slasher isn't the logical conclusion of the Abbey. The bottom of the slippery slope: First Werewolves, then Witches, then Humans. A Slasher is as far from the archetypal Abbey Hunter as it is from the archetypal Union Hunter. (Which is to say both Compacts produce Slashers).<br /> <br /> Obviously you could create some Hedonistic Undertaking with a Frailty like can't use the same MO twice; but honestly that kind of feels like a Round Peg Square Hole sort of deal. Hunters are probably the most diverse splat, the ways they fall would be pretty diverse too. IMO an Abby Hunter is more likely to end up Claimed by an Infernal Demon attracted to their over indulgence of Vice than a Slasher.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think this is probably my chief reason for not being too keen on Abby-&gt;Slashers. I'm very much a theme first kind of guy, and the Abby's theme is immoral hedonistic novelty seekers. Slashers are creatures of habit. These are clearly very different themes.<br /> <br /> Even if the logical in-universe conclusion of the Abby's immorality is Slasherdom, I'd rather find some way to preserve that theme. Redefining immoral as &quot;I won't let morals stop me having fun&quot; instead of &quot;Lets do the most depraved stuff we can!&quot; is my way of preserving the Abby's theme. Plus, I do think it would genuinely be an improvement.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> After typing this I'm reminded that The Hunt Club don't actually fit the above. But then I always liked the idea that the Hunt Club were non-Slasher serial killers, mostly because I could never figure out what Undertaking could actually qualify for membership.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790951#post790951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people seem to be coming at Hunter as if they're supposed to be the good guys, or it's the 'good guy' game, without any room for anything else. Is that how you see it Hunter the Vigil? How you think second edition should be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Hunter should be the 'good guy' game. But there should be a game with a few good guy Splats you might play as. The Union and the Lucifuge for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791023#post791023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now this I could totally get behind. Maybe shift that aspect over to the Hunt Club, and make it one of the reasons an Abbey member might turn Slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't see this working.<br /> <br /> The Club are all about rules, regulation, and murder as performance art. An Abbey member jumping to the Club because they want more opportunities to indulge one's passions doesn't fit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-22-2015, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T14:03:31-08:00","id":791074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791071#post791071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some further thoughts.<br /> <br /> I can't see this working.<br /> <br /> The Club are all about rules, regulation, and murder as performance art. An Abbey member jumping to the Club because they want more opportunities to indulge one's passions doesn't fit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T15:01:10-08:00","id":791106,"title":"","content":"As things stand now, I consider the Abbey a bit of a missed opportunity. While the other Hunter organizations have aspects that can cast them in both good and bad light, Ashwood Abbey's presentation doubled down on the negative. I think &quot;Compacts and Conspiracies&quot; made a step in the right direction, by showing their thrill seeking as not necessarily repugnant.<br /> <br /> There aren't many hunters who would be willing to actually socialize with the monsters or to spend the night in a haunted locale just for kicks. Trying to make friends with monsters opens up many possibilities plot-wise, which trying to kill them - doesn't. With a greater network to fund their activities, advise them on the consequences and stage an intervention should things go too far, these Hunters could accomplish successes and cause disasters unthinkable in other organisations. Each story shared with the whole of the Compact would warn the members what not to do, or more likely, how to do damage control.<br /> <br /> So far, the Abbey only gets close to tackling these themes. Their descriptions are overly focused on murder and decadence. Curiously, the Compact has potential to be one of the most diplomatic in its dealings with monsters, since once they start interacting socially with the supernatural, they appear on it's radar and can be held accountable. On the other hand, with their connections, experience and the proverbial &quot;big stick&quot;, they can try to hold their own against manipulation. That is not to say everything is pleasant. Diplomacy can be really cutthroat, especially with monsters on one side and thrill-seekers on the other.<br /> <br /> This approach to the Vigil deserves more attention. Both expanding on the Abbey and creating a new Compact based around it are acceptable means to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:24:14-08:00","id":791144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791071#post791071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some further thoughts.<br /> <br /> Slashers don't actually fit the Abbey that well. A Slasher is defined by compulsion, and being a creature of very strict habits. Look at the Legend Undertaking for the most obvious example, or <i>VASCU Case study : \u201cNone\u201d</i>. The Abbey strike me as the exact opposite, always on a quest for novelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly enough, it's just that fact that has me thinking that the Abbey wouldn't counted as a &quot;Slasher&quot; due to low breaking points but rather they would find humans prey far too... boring.<br /> <br /> They exist for a wealth of experiences and try to make each one more unique and more flavorful than the last. The Supernatural provides that in spades in a way that normal mortals simply can't.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T17:35:03-08:00","id":791172,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>Which of these three options do you prefer and why?</li> </ul><br /> I'm lax to have the Abbey as antagonists <b>only</b>. I think no change or blending the two would be my own preference. The Abbey was honestly one of my favourite groups in 1e and I'd like to see them still playable, if updated so they fit more with the rest of product. However, the reason I liked them to begin with because of the whole vibe they had of being dispicably extravagent and sadistic as Hunters, doing it for sport and taking actual enjoyment out of what they did... It was a nice break from the more serious groups and led to some fun PCs.<ul><li>If you\u2019re worried about a change, what is your hangup and how do you feel this\u2019ll affect your group?</li> </ul><br /> I'm worried about playing an Abbey character to be made 'stressful', having the PC be watched over, a lack of trust which is really detrimental to Hunter games, due to Tactics. I'd rather that over having them unplayable though, if pushed. Although having the Abbey play up and be gloriously unrepetant Slashers would be great, but playable. I really don't want such a unique group removed.<ul><li>If you\u2019re excited by a specific idea, what do you like most about it?</li> </ul><br /> I like the addition of the Hunt Club as antagonists. Overall I like the 'Blending of the Two' option, especially for the story-hooks it provides.<ul><li>If you already play Hunter, are Tier Two chronicles your preferred style of gameplay?</li> </ul><br /> Tier Two and Tier Three for my games. I like the addition perks that these higher tiers give. It feels more like playing a splat than a mortal hunter game that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:06:54-08:00","id":791182,"title":"","content":"An organization of rich murderous rapists shouldn't be a playable option in anything short of a Black Dog product and their existence allows shitty players to excuse their behavior as being in the spirit of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:12:31-08:00","id":791184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791182#post791182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An organization of rich murderous rapists shouldn't be a playable option in anything short of a Black Dog product and their existence allows shitty players to excuse their behavior as being in the spirit of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Ashwood can stay, but aspects will have to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:16:45-08:00","id":791189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791182#post791182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An organization of rich murderous rapists shouldn't be a playable option in anything short of a Black Dog product and their existence allows shitty players to excuse their behavior as being in the spirit of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't really see how one can differentiate this group from so many other playable groups in so many of these games. Are vampires less murderous and rapey because they aren't human anymore? I can understand the distaste from the current material out there about the Abbey. I don't think that there is any worth though calling out a valid attempt to create a group that struggles with very difficult parts of our psychology. Instead of looking at it as trash to be thrown out, imagine how cool it would be if someone developed a story and a character where the Abbey really made the other characters struggle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:19:23-08:00","id":791192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791033#post791033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically I think that the Abbey should be the Hunter group with the inside track when it comes to getting information from other Supernaturals. And the cool parties that everyone, even the Prince, would like to receive an invite to.</div> </div> </div> </div>If people are okay with a vampire prince hunting ghouls for sport then I think we can present Ashwood Abbey as not just a compact of slashers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:30:11-08:00","id":791196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791189#post791189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see how one can differentiate this group from so many other playable groups in so many of these games. Are vampires less murderous and rapey because they aren't human anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been explicitly stated that vampires need the Blush of Life to engage in sexual intercourse, that it is &quot;cold&quot; for them, and that it pales in comparison to the Kiss. The legit sexually violent vampire is the minority, not the rule. So vampires are less rapey because of several logical, valid reasons, not because of arbitrariness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791189#post791189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of looking at it as trash to be thrown out, imagine how cool it would be if someone developed a story and a character where the Abbey really made the other characters struggle.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is exactly what antagonists do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:50:02-08:00","id":791203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791196#post791196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been explicitly stated that vampires need the Blush of Life to engage in sexual intercourse, that it is &quot;cold&quot; for them, and that it pales in comparison to the Kiss. The legit sexually violent vampire is the minority, not the rule. So vampires are less rapey because of several logical, valid reasons, not because of arbitrariness.<br /> <br /> That is a really solid point. It is also the case that people that are members of groups that enact unethical acts are still culpable to some extent even if they themselves didn't act. This is all just splitting hairs though. I guess a better example would be the other compacts and conspiracies (Wouldn't it be completely reasonable to have a Taskforce Valkyrie soldier be a rapist, or, murderer considering how prevalent that is in the military). All of them could be easily twisted to be unethical and amoral. It is not really up to fiction to be completely in taste with those that consume it.<br /> <br /> Rape and murder are terrible things. No one is arguing that, but what is the value in saying that this fictional setting which is steeped in the horror's of humanity is not the place where we can deal with the what if of being those monsters. It weakens the fictional strength of the setting.<br /> <br /> I agree that as the Abbey is written now is not very nuanced, but that doesn't mean the concept can't be in the coming edition. If this isn't for you personally I understand and there are ways of easily dealing with that in your group.<br /> <br /> And this is exactly what antagonists do.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. This doesn't negate a player character doing the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T18:50:38-08:00","id":791204,"title":"","content":"This accidently posted in quote.<br /> <br /> That is a really solid point. It is also the case that people that are members of groups that enact unethical acts are still culpable to some extent even if they themselves didn't act. This is all just splitting hairs though. I guess a better example would be the other compacts and conspiracies (Wouldn't it be completely reasonable to have a Taskforce Valkyrie soldier be a rapist, or, murderer considering how prevalent that is in the military). All of them could be easily twisted to be unethical and amoral. It is not really up to fiction to be completely in taste with those that consume it.<br /> <br /> Rape and murder are terrible things. No one is arguing that, but what is the value in saying that this fictional setting which is steeped in the horror's of humanity is not the place where we can deal with the what if of being those monsters. It weakens the fictional strength of the setting.<br /> <br /> I agree that as the Abbey is written now is not very nuanced, but that doesn't mean the concept can't be in the coming edition. If this isn't for you personally I understand and there are ways of easily dealing with that in your group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:00:25-08:00","id":791212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791204#post791204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. This doesn't negate a player character doing the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it doesn't. It seems to be some sort of unspoken assumption that antagonists are off-limits for players, when there's no logical reason for that to be the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791204#post791204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a really solid point. It is also the case that people that are members of groups that enact unethical acts are still culpable to some extent even if they themselves didn't act. This is all just splitting hairs though. I guess a better example would be the other compacts and conspiracies (Wouldn't it be completely reasonable to have a Taskforce Valkyrie soldier be a rapist, or, murderer considering how prevalent that is in the military). All of them could be easily twisted to be unethical and amoral. It is not really up to fiction to be completely in taste with those that consume it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: They are exceptions. The Ashwood Abbey has, <i>as an institutional ethos</i>, the use of sexual violence for their own thrill-seeking ends. They even say it themselves that the sexual violence isn't even a goal unto itself, but a mean to exert power upon others. There is a <i>very important difference</i> between bad apples and an entire institution that indoctrinates its members into sexual violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791204#post791204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rape and murder are terrible things. No one is arguing that, but what is the value in saying that this fictional setting which is steeped in the horror's of humanity is not the place where we can deal with the what if of being those monsters. It weakens the fictional strength of the setting.<br /> <br /> I agree that as the Abbey is written now is not very nuanced, but that doesn't mean the concept can't be in the coming edition. If this isn't for you personally I understand and there are ways of easily dealing with that in your group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not talking about murder. I have never criticised the Ashwood Abbey's propensity for murder. I am exclusively talking about the sexual violence angle, which crosses a line that many groups are not willing to deal with. There is <i>an entire Abyss of difference</i> between rape and murder. They're not just crimes on a list, numbers on a legal code. They are drastically different experiences.<br /> <br /> Nobody is forbidding players from being rapists if that's the kind of game they want to have at the table. It's simply placing them as antagonists and dedicating less book space to them.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, we've dealt with it since it was published. We've instantly relegated them to the realm of antagonists with but a thought. I would very much appreciate the addition of a different compact in their stead. I mean, this way, we all get what we want. The Ashwood Abbey is still in the book, just elsewhere, and the rest of us get another compact to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:01:17-08:00","id":791213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791204#post791204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rape and murder are terrible things. No one is arguing that, but what is the value in saying that this fictional setting which is steeped in the horror's of humanity is not the place where we can deal with the what if of being those monsters. It weakens the fictional strength of the setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't trust the average roleplayer with a nuanced masterpiece of storytelling. Giving them a green light on playing rapists is not going to let us explore the 'horrors of humanity,' it's just going to ruin game night for a few groups and make the Vigil setting an unsafe place for players.<br /> <br /> This sounds frighteningly like the &quot;racism has a place in the World of Darkness, because racism is dark!&quot; debate I've had to endlessly wrestle over the last decade, and I won't have it if it's at all possible to avoid it.<br /> <br /> Moral grey is &quot;are we better than the monsters we hunt?&quot;<br /> <br /> Moral grey is not &quot;me and my friends are rich serial killers who don't care for consent.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:13:56-08:00","id":791220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791213#post791213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't trust the average roleplayer with a nuanced masterpiece of storytelling. Giving them a green light on playing rapists is not going to let us explore the 'horrors of humanity,' it's just going to ruin game night for a few groups and make the Vigil setting an unsafe place for players.<br /> <br /> This sounds frighteningly like the &quot;racism has a place in the World of Darkness, because racism is dark!&quot; debate I've had to endlessly wrestle over the last decade, and I won't have it if it's at all possible to avoid it.<br /> <br /> Moral grey is &quot;are we better than the monsters we hunt?&quot;<br /> <br /> Moral grey is not &quot;me and my friends are rich serial killers who don't care for consent.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> This really isn't the place to have a conversation about the issues that come up in our play groups. Nor is it a place to talk about the politics of fiction, what it depicts and why. I can completely hear all of the valid points you are making.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a more useful way of dealing with this issue isn't just with dealing with this individual game, but in having the developers making a decision about how it defines what is appropriate for its fiction and the playable characters that come out of it as a whole. At least with some clear boundaries hopefully these conversations can go more smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:37:28-08:00","id":791234,"title":"","content":"I want to clarify that when I said that this is not the place to talk about those things I only meant that discussion boards are poor replacement for in person conversations about the things are emotionally hard for us. There is no way for anyone to understand the context with which the other comes from. Things like gender, personal history, and age, are left behind.<br /> <br /> In no way did I want to support the pain of women anywhere. I chose my words poorly.<br /> <br /> Heres to this thread resolving this conflict in a way that is both ehtical and interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:51:01-08:00","id":791242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791212#post791212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again: They are exceptions. The Ashwood Abbey has, <i>as an institutional ethos</i>, the use of sexual violence for their own thrill-seeking ends. They even say it themselves that the sexual violence isn't even a goal unto itself, but a mean to exert power upon others. There is a <i>very important difference</i> between bad apples and an entire institution that indoctrinates its members into sexual violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's inaccurate. They are hedonists, but it's clear their idea of pleasure is not solely focused on sex, consensual or not. An entire faction is devoted to finding out 'what is possible' in the supernatural world, and another with more of a competitive sporting angle focusing on the hunt itself. The Libertines faction is the one focused on breaking taboos, and even they aren't called out as solely being sexual predators.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey is often linked to sexual debauchery and rape, but rape is not a prerequisite nor something every member has taken part of. Compacts and Conspiracies even mentions this, 'It's perhaps tempting to think of them as hunters devoted to hedonistic sex - and they can be, often basking in all its faux-pagan trappings - but really, they play with monsters the same way kings once toyed with commoners; it's a rush to ruin lives, to break hearts, to put yourself in mortal danger to remind yourself that you're not a god and that you are very much still human.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:53:40-08:00","id":791244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=790986#post790986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have fun. They don't worry about the moral issues. They're good at what they do, and do it proudly. They celebrate their victories.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's almost a textbook description of a Psychopath.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:00:30-08:00","id":791247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791244#post791244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's almost a textbook description of a Psychopath.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>And football players. And movie producers. And werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-22-2015, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:04:22-08:00","id":791249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791244#post791244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's almost a textbook description of a Psychopath.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of true. No psychological organization uses that term diagnostically. If you look at the research on the prevalence of antisocial personality disorder, it is found in a large percentage of incarcerated individuals and can be found in corporate executives. This is even more complicated by the debate about whether certain counter culture, or, revolutionary, actions would fall under diagnostic criteria for this illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:07:26-08:00","id":791251,"title":"","content":"I make note of antisocial personality disorder not because they should be construed as the same, but simply that it shares the highest level of comorbidity (likehood that an incidence of one will occur with the other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:15:06-08:00","id":791253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791011#post791011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that in both these cases, the sexual element of the Ashwood Abbey has been completely abandoned. This is absolutely crucial. I don't think I or any of my players could stomach a group that enacts sexual violence on anyone (even monsters) and isn't an antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791182#post791182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An organization of rich murderous rapists shouldn't be a playable option in anything short of a Black Dog product and their existence allows shitty players to excuse their behavior as being in the spirit of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>THIS. I could never accept the Abbey as protagonists as long as the sexual element remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 12-22-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:41:24-08:00","id":791268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791242#post791242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's inaccurate. They are hedonists, but it's clear their idea of pleasure is not solely focused on sex, consensual or not. An entire faction is devoted to finding out 'what is possible' in the supernatural world, and another with more of a competitive sporting angle focusing on the hunt itself. The Libertines faction is the one focused on breaking taboos, and even they aren't called out as solely being sexual predators.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey is often linked to sexual debauchery and rape, but rape is not a prerequisite nor something every member has taken part of. Compacts and Conspiracies even mentions this, 'It's perhaps tempting to think of them as hunters devoted to hedonistic sex - and they can be, often basking in all its faux-pagan trappings - but really, they play with monsters the same way kings once toyed with commoners; it's a rush to ruin lives, to break hearts, to put yourself in mortal danger to remind yourself that you're not a god and that you are very much still human.'</div> </div> </div> </div>The Compacts and Conspiracies book explicitly describes the use of sexual violence as a means to an end: exerting power and dominance over whatever the Abbey has captured. People keep assuming that those who criticise the sexual element mistakenly buy into the &quot;hedonistic rapist&quot; stereotype and just &quot;don't get it&quot; or &quot;don't see the full picture.&quot; We (or at least I) know better than that. We know that the Ashwood Abbey is more than that that, that it uses sexual violence as a tool rather than an end. However, <i>it is still a group that specifically encourages the use of sexual violence on helpless victims.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:54:31-08:00","id":791274,"title":"","content":"I am going to go with opition 3 primarly on the basis that it will give us a new compact, especially one that is non-western. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:57:07-08:00","id":791276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791268#post791268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Compacts and Conspiracies book explicitly describes the use of sexual violence as a means to an end: exerting power and dominance over whatever the Abbey has captured. People keep assuming that those who criticise the sexual element mistakenly buy into the &quot;hedonistic rapist&quot; stereotype and just &quot;don't get it&quot; or &quot;don't see the full picture.&quot; We (or at least I) know better than that. We know that the Ashwood Abbey is more than that that, that it uses sexual violence as a tool rather than an end. However, <i>it is still a group that specifically encourages the use of sexual violence on helpless victims.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at my copy of Compacts and Conspiracies right now and I don't see it.<br /> <br /> From p10, 'And play with monsters, they do. The definition of \u201cplay\u201d varies from cell to cell, club to club. They\u2019ve earned a reputation as rapists and monsters, and for some, that\u2019s certainly true \u2014 but for most, it\u2019s about the thrill of the thing. They already have power. What they don\u2019t possess is excitement \u2014 at society\u2019s upper echelons, ennui is a persistent threat, and the Abbey offers ways to combat that boredom.<br /> ...<br /> One cell holds parties. Small affairs \u2014 salons, really. They invite one monster, maybe three. They don\u2019t kill them. Maybe they drug them. If sex occurs, it\u2019s consensual \u2014 some are happy with orgies, with all that flesh slapping and smooth hands pawing, while others prefer to host spaces away from the salons where its members can go and nuzzle the neck of a vampire or suck the tongue of some cackling demon.<br /> Another club has a big, lavish affair \u2014 string quartet, a handful of cherry-picked celebrities and executives, a $10,000 food spread. At midnight they open the cages, free the doped-up captives and hunt them on horses (or golf-carts, or in their Maseratis).<br /> A cell in Chicago gets a thrill just from hanging out with monsters\u2014when the vampire feeds, they feed, when the pack hunts, they go with them and work backup.'<br /> <br /> And who 'keeps assuming' that those who criticize the sexual element 'just don't get it?' I haven't seen a single post about that, though I stopped reading the last page halfway down. Several posts on this page have called the entire compact rapists, which is simply not accurate.<br /> <br /> While it's true that there are members that are rapists, it's not the focus of the Ashwood as a whole. It's not even the focus of the Libertines and is called out in the first book as not setting the standard for the rest. And while I agree that the sexual predator aspect should be toned down, they're not nearly as commonplace as people are making it seem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2015, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T20:57:39-08:00","id":791277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791234#post791234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to clarify that when I said that this is not the place to talk about those things I only meant that discussion boards are poor replacement for in person conversations about the things are emotionally hard for us. There is no way for anyone to understand the context with which the other comes from. Things like gender, personal history, and age, are left behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're trying to say here, but I'm still going to disagree with you. This is the place to talk about exactly these issues and to try and force ourselves to understand (or at least consider) what the pov of other posters may be. <br /> <br /> Here's the thing. One of the reasons I'm so hellbent to make it through the Open Call and write for this book is because I believe in Onyx Path. They have made concerted efforts to build a series of games in CofD that are dark, grim, and horrific, but in a way that the game itself is still extremely supportive of the people playing it. A lot of this has been in the form of representation and diversisty, but there has been a less obvious side to it too. Things like the Unihar from WtF have been removed, in that case because it was an unnecessary aspect that cased great pain to individuals who have experienced complications with childbirth. The systematized sexual abuse of the Abbey is another egrigious aspect of CofD that can and should be removed. It's not something acceptable as a player option, because it implicitly normalizes sexual abuse, even if that is not the intent of the players or designers of the games. If the Unihar went, so does this aspect of the Abbey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:04:33-08:00","id":791281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791268#post791268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We (or at least I) know better than that. We know that the Ashwood Abbey is more than that that, that it uses sexual violence as a tool rather than an end. However, <i>it is still a group that specifically encourages the use of sexual violence on helpless victims.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So very much this.<br /> <br /> I don't care if most of the Abbey aren't into the sexual stuff. As long as the organization actively encourages sexual violence, it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Just because you're not a rapist, you're not redeemable if you're cheerleading for rapists.<br /> <br /> The Abbey doesn't institutionally turn a blind eye to the hedonistic sexpots in its ranks. It treats skilled users of sexual violence as much of model members as skilled users of physical violence. There's no escaping that with any amount of, &quot;well not all members do it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:06:30-08:00","id":791282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791281#post791281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So very much this.<br /> <br /> I don't care if most of the Abbey aren't into the sexual stuff. As long as the organization actively encourages sexual violence, it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Just because you're not a rapist, you're not redeemable if you're cheerleading for rapists.<br /> <br /> The Abbey doesn't institutionally turn a blind eye to the hedonistic sexpots in its ranks. It treats skilled users of sexual violence as much of model members as skilled users of physical violence. There's no escaping that with any amount of, &quot;well not all members do it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually pointed out in the section on the Libertines in the core book that they don't approve, or at the least aren't cheerleaders. 'A lot of the things they do revolt even the members of the Abbey.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2015, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:22:18-08:00","id":791298,"title":"","content":"Y'know, I talk a lot of shit about the WoD/CofD fandom for being pretty terrible. This thread gives me hope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791274#post791274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to go with opition 3 primarly on the basis that it will give us a new compact, especially one that is non-western. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Right on the money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:24:20-08:00","id":791300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791276#post791276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm looking at my copy of Compacts and Conspiracies right now and I don't see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss the actual fluff of the Ashwood Abbey in Compacts and Conspiracies?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Make no mistake! You are an important person. You have money. People like you. That\u2019s why you\u2019re here. That\u2019s why you\u2019re holding that knife and that rope. You deserve more money. You deserve more love and more fame. You are a creature of privilege, and you can do anything you want. Once I open this door, you\u2019ll see what waits on the other side on the chaise. <b>You can do anything you want to him. It\u2019s not about sex, though it can be. It\u2019s about power. It\u2019s about pleasure. And most importantly, it\u2019s about privilege.</b>&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The organisation explicitly encourages the use of sexual violence as a way to demonstrate privilege and obtain pleasure by subjugating and victimising others. If you happen to enjoy the sex itself, hey, bonus. But this is an explicit example of the Ashwood Abbey introducing a potential new member and making it absolutely clear that &quot;anything goes, especially the sex.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:24:41-08:00","id":791302,"title":"","content":"I made a comment in the blog, but I'll bring up the general idea for discussion here.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't use the book's real estate to position them as a PC Compact (I think that space could be better spent on something new), but I wouldn't turn them into full-blown villains either (as that could detract from the moral relativism inherent in the game).<br /> <br /> I think making them an organization that has an unnaturally high slasher conversion rate could make them both better suited as an antagonist and more interesting for exploration by Abbey PCs. Other compacts are starting to tag them potentially as a looming threat, but you also have concern within the organization itself, as paranoia runs rampant. They've lost a chapter house and maybe more to former members gone berserk, and there's the feeling among Abbey members that anyone could turn. What structure of leadership exists is weak at the moment and prone to overthrow. I like the idea of the Abbey sitting at a precipice. There's a chance for reform, but there's also the threat of total implosion or of being dismantled by outside forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:25:54-08:00","id":791303,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791268#post791268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Compacts and Conspiracies book explicitly describes the use of sexual violence as a means to an end: exerting power and dominance over whatever the Abbey has captured. People keep assuming that those who criticise the sexual element mistakenly buy into the &quot;hedonistic rapist&quot; stereotype and just &quot;don't get it&quot; or &quot;don't see the full picture.&quot; We (or at least I) know better than that. We know that the Ashwood Abbey is more than that that, that it uses sexual violence as a tool rather than an end. However, <i>it is still a group that specifically encourages the use of sexual violence on helpless victims.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I can't see any quotes that support that the Ashwood Abbey specifically encourages the use of sexual violence on helpless victims. Here are the quotes I found from the Compacts and Conspiracies book that address that topic:<br /> <br /> From the intro (pg 10) &quot;They\u2019ve earned a reputation as rapists and monsters, and for some, that\u2019s certainly true\u2014but for most, it\u2019s about the thrill of the thing. They already have power. What they don\u2019t possess is excitement..&quot;<br /> <br /> That's then followed by the tactics of five cells none of which use sexual violence. There is a reference to them drugging some supernaturals to attend their parties but that section also specifically states that if sex occurs (implying it's not a given), then it's consensual. I think my favorite of the tactics is the one in Bangkok where the cell toys with a supernatural, teases them, attacks them and then runs like hell to see if they can get away in a really dangerous version of Tag and Go Seek.<br /> <br /> Description of Libertines (pg 13): They have a reputation within the compact as being rapists and perverts. The latter is largely true, the former, less so. The Libertines are interested in wearing down the walls between social norms and mores; it\u2019s much more fun to bring others along for the ride willingly.&quot;<br /> <br /> If there are any quotes that state the organization as a group does specifically encourage sexual violence please tell me the page number as I don't see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:27:39-08:00","id":791305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791029#post791029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is almost as if the Developer wants to hear from people playing Hunter and get their thoughts on some complex parts of the game...<br /> <br /> -MMM</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know, right?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:32:16-08:00","id":791308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vedic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791303#post791303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I can't see any quotes that support that the Ashwood Abbey specifically encourages the use of sexual violence on helpless victims. Here are the quotes I found from the Compacts and Conspiracies book that address that topic:</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 10, paragraph to the left, in the special font. Starts with &quot;Make no mistake!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:34:03-08:00","id":791309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791300#post791300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you miss the actual fluff of the Ashwood Abbey in Compacts and Conspiracies?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Make no mistake! You are an important person. You have money. People like you. That\u2019s why you\u2019re here. That\u2019s why you\u2019re holding that knife and that rope. You deserve more money. You deserve more love and more fame. You are a creature of privilege, and you can do anything you want. Once I open this door, you\u2019ll see what waits on the other side on the chaise. <b>You can do anything you want to him. It\u2019s not about sex, though it can be. It\u2019s about power. It\u2019s about pleasure. And most importantly, it\u2019s about privilege.</b>&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The organisation explicitly encourages the use of sexual violence as a way to demonstrate privilege and obtain pleasure by subjugating and victimising others. If you happen to enjoy the sex itself, hey, bonus. But this is an explicit example of the Ashwood Abbey introducing a potential new member and making it absolutely clear that &quot;anything goes, especially the sex.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So if one member of a group says it's not about sex but it can be but what it mainly is is about power and privilege when the rest of the section specifically says sexually violent members are a minority that translates into the group as a whole encourages it? I'm sorry, I don't see the validity of that argument. I mean, there are a lot of nasty aspects to the Ashwood Abbey that could be criticized but I think a stronger argument could be made by focusing on the parts the book actually does state.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","user":"Vedic","date":". 12-23-2015, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:36:12-08:00","id":791310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791300#post791300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you miss the actual fluff of the Ashwood Abbey in Compacts and Conspiracies?<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Make no mistake! You are an important person. You have money. People like you. That\u2019s why you\u2019re here. That\u2019s why you\u2019re holding that knife and that rope. You deserve more money. You deserve more love and more fame. You are a creature of privilege, and you can do anything you want. Once I open this door, you\u2019ll see what waits on the other side on the chaise. <b>You can do anything you want to him. It\u2019s not about sex, though it can be. It\u2019s about power. It\u2019s about pleasure. And most importantly, it\u2019s about privilege.</b>&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. The organisation explicitly encourages the use of sexual violence as a way to demonstrate privilege and obtain pleasure by subjugating and victimising others. If you happen to enjoy the sex itself, hey, bonus. But this is an explicit example of the Ashwood Abbey introducing a potential new member and making it absolutely clear that &quot;anything goes, especially the sex.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hate to give you ammo for the old 'I told you so' gun, but I do think this is a matter of you not getting it. <br /> <br /> While the Abbey is certainly about getting pleasure from the the hunt and the monsters they victimize, the organization as a whole does not encourage the use of sexual violence for that matter. You have the actual write-up saying this, and even in your quote the character says it's not about sex, and furthermore explaining what the power is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:39:14-08:00","id":791312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791277#post791277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're trying to say here, but I'm still going to disagree with you. This is the place to talk about exactly these issues and to try and force ourselves to understand (or at least consider) what the pov of other posters may be.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. One of the reasons I'm so hellbent to make it through the Open Call and write for this book is because I believe in Onyx Path. They have made concerted efforts to build a series of games in CofD that are dark, grim, and horrific, but in a way that the game itself is still extremely supportive of the people playing it. A lot of this has been in the form of representation and diversisty, but there has been a less obvious side to it too. Things like the Unihar from WtF have been removed, in that case because it was an unnecessary aspect that cased great pain to individuals who have experienced complications with childbirth. The systematized sexual abuse of the Abbey is another egrigious aspect of CofD that can and should be removed. It's not something acceptable as a player option, because it implicitly normalizes sexual abuse, even if that is not the intent of the players or designers of the games. If the Unihar went, so does this aspect of the Abbey.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think what is hard with that personally then is that I currently work in a field and have personally been affected by rape in such a way that it has left me theoretically divergent from most people. I know my views aren't common about how we need to approach it, but I am in complete support of building a product that is inclusive above all else.<br /> <br /> I agree that we should try and I think working with the developers to set forth boundaries would be a positive step forward. I say that because we aren't aware of what other conflicts will arise in the future with other products and I think there are better ways than waiting for them to be brought up on the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:42:36-08:00","id":791314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vedic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791309#post791309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if one member of a group says it's not about sex but it can be but what it mainly is is about power and privilege when the rest of the section specifically sexually violent members are a minority that translates into the group as a whole encourages it? I'm sorry, I don't see the validity of that argument. I mean, there are a lot of nasty aspects to the Ashwood Abbey that could be criticized but I think a stronger argument could be made by focusing on the parts the book actually does state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will repeat myself again: Just because the sexual violence is not the goal doesn't mean it doesn't exist. It still happens, it just serves as a means rather than an end.<br /> <br /> Note that the bit you're so casually disregarding is what the writers chose to represent the Ashwood Abbey <i>in-universe.</i> Whether or not you consider relevant or not, the writers felt that the inclusion of sexual violence in the in-universe quote (and, in addition, the mention of the Ashwood Abbey's unique mechanic as a way to represent sexual parties, which clearly states <i>&quot;while others check their restraint at the door and wade into the fray with naught but harlequin masks, Taser weapons and tumescent flesh.&quot;</i> (p.14). The writers further that point when they state <i>&quot;this isn\u2019t necessarily about running the mechanics of an Ashwood Abbey sex party (though it can be!),&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Over and over, the theme of sexual violence in the Ashwood Abbey keeps cropping up. The writers felt it important for the Ashwood Abbey to have its theme of sexual violence remarked upon several times throughout the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791310#post791310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to give you ammo for the old 'I told you so' gun, but I do think this is a matter of you not getting it.<br /> <br /> While the Abbey is certainly about getting pleasure from the the hunt and the monsters they victimize, the organization as a whole does not encourage the use of sexual violence for that matter. You have the actual write-up saying this, and even in your quote the character says it's not about sex, and furthermore explaining what the power is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna have to state it again: <i>It doesn't matter if sex is not the point. The Ashwood Abbey's in-universe write-up canonically encourages the use of sexual violence. It literally doesn't matter what the point is of that sexual violence is.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":10056,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","user":"ShadowKnight1224","date":". 12-23-2015, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:49:29-08:00","id":791319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791314#post791314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writers felt it important for the Ashwood Abbey to have its theme of sexual violence remarked upon several times throughout the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>That ledge you're on is getting smaller and smaller.<br /> <br /> Not all members of AA engage in devious sexual activity. What part of this do you not understand? Some do. Most don't. There are actual organizations(without the supernatural hunting part) like this all over the world. The world sucks. But this is elitism, sadism, cruelty, with a hint of sexual deviance wrapped into one $$$ package. If it's something you don't want to use with your gaming group, don't use it.<br /> <br /> When Chuck Wendig and company wrote the original, I don't remember there being this much question into AA and their background. I've seen a number of AA characters played to perfection. Some, not so much. Like with ANY game. <br /> <br /> Why is this any different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:53:37-08:00","id":791321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791312#post791312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think what is hard with that personally then is that I currently work in a field and have personally been affected by rape in such a way that it has left me theoretically divergent from most people. I know my views aren't common about how we need to approach it, but I am in complete support of building a product that is inclusive above all else.<br /> <br /> I agree that we should try and I think working with the developers to set forth boundaries would be a positive step forward. I say that because we aren't aware of what other conflicts will arise in the future with other products and I think there are better ways than waiting for them to be brought up on the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. But that's also part of the Open Dev process. Monica isn't waiting for them to be brought up. She's asking use to bring them up and have a discourse. Are there flaws? Totally, the internet lacks as a communication tool. But it still has great value, and I think it's better to discuss these points of contention in any medium to inform the development of the product than let them become an elephant in the room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:53:46-08:00","id":791322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791314#post791314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will repeat myself again: Just because the sexual violence is not the goal doesn't mean it doesn't exist. It still happens, it just serves as a means rather than an end.<br /> <br /> Note that the bit you're so casually disregarding is what the writers chose to represent the Ashwood Abbey <i>in-universe.</i> Whether or not you consider relevant or not, the writers felt that the inclusion of sexual violence in the in-universe quote (and, in addition, the mention of the Ashwood Abbey's unique mechanic as a way to represent sexual parties, which clearly states <i>&quot;while others check their restraint at the door and wade into the fray with naught but harlequin masks, Taser weapons and tumescent flesh.&quot;</i> (p.14). The writers further that point when they state <i>&quot;this isn\u2019t necessarily about running the mechanics of an Ashwood Abbey sex party (though it can be!),&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> Over and over, the theme of sexual violence in the Ashwood Abbey keeps cropping up. The writers felt it important for the Ashwood Abbey to have its theme of sexual violence remarked upon several times throughout the text.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Gonna have to state it again: <i>It doesn't matter if sex is not the point. The Ashwood Abbey's in-universe write-up canonically encourages the use of sexual violence. It literally doesn't matter what the point is of that sexual violence is.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>If you changed the word canonically to tolerates in your last three sentences then you would have a much better argument. I'm not casually disregarding anything by the way; I'm taking an introduction that was specifically portrayed as one member and reading the rest of the text to state what the entire group as a whole is portrayed as instead of only the part that supports my point of view. I'm not disagreeing that having some members who are like that is a problematic part of the Ashwood Abbey that might be better shunted off to their members that join the Hunt Club or are on their way there; I'm disagreeing that the book canonically states what you're saying it does as it states the opposite. Now you can certainly make the argument that a group that tolerates any members that do that is not a group you feel comfortable with being portrayed in the protagonist section but stating something the book does not, in my opinion, just leads to a more inflamed discussion that is less productive in the long run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","user":"Vedic","date":". 12-23-2015, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:54:05-08:00","id":791323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791314#post791314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over and over, the theme of sexual violence in the Ashwood Abbey keeps cropping up. The writers felt it important for the Ashwood Abbey to have its theme of sexual violence remarked upon several times throughout the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's inaccurate. The rape angle actually pops up just in Witch Finders and Compacts and Conspiracies, and in the latter is focused on one faction of the group. Are the Union all racist terrorists?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gonna have to state it again: <i>It doesn't matter if sex is not the point. The Ashwood Abbey's in-universe write-up canonically encourages the use of sexual violence. It literally doesn't matter what the point is of that sexual violence is.</i> </div> </div> </div>And again, it doesn't. One character says you can do anything. The rest of the write-up explains that they are not all rapists.<br /> <br /> Certainly it should be toned down, have it be clear that the Abbey doesn't condone it, especially considering the risks. But since it isn't as commonplace as you think it should be easy to remove. The writer of that section of Witch Finders really ran with the sexual angle, though the Night Stalkers write-up didn't mention sex at all and the Spirit Stalkers section on the Abbey used the competitors angle, with hunters getting close to werewolves by trying to date them before revealing who they were and, ideally, killing before being killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T22:00:15-08:00","id":791327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791321#post791321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. But that's also part of the Open Dev process. Monica isn't waiting for them to be brought up. She's asking use to bring them up and have a discourse. Are there flaws? Totally, the internet lacks as a communication tool. But it still has great value, and I think it's better to discuss these points of contention in any medium to inform the development of the product than let them become an elephant in the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with you. You are right about this process. It is interesting how much my current play groups handling of the material differs in its understanding. That has in turn lead to me saying things that I know were not right.<br /> <br /> My suggestion about working with developers is perhaps to have a separate discussion focused on what the community wants to make as overarching boundaries. Hopefully that clears up my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T22:00:18-08:00","id":791328,"title":"","content":"I like to mention that Option 3 would give us a new compact, one that is from a non-western country, ie Brazil, Nigeria, or Japan. That is my main reason for picking option 3. If I want the Ashwood Abby, I still have them from the core book, but here I would have another group to use and that is good IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T22:00:37-08:00","id":791329,"title":"","content":"Adrenaline is ecstatic. Honesty is refreshing. The risk of losing sight of the lines is the stuff of epic stories.<br /> <br /> I like the AA, despite everything that makes me squick-and this is coming from a guy who goes from chill to violent at the suggestion of sexual violence, mind. But Ashwood gets to certain ugly truths that are at the core of any Hunter, and gets right to the hard questions: not only why people become terrible, but how we handle desire and power fantasy. If anything, Ashwood criticizes the justifications of Hunter flat out, and asks players to ask questions about play experiences: why do we enjoy a game about hunting monsters, tearing apart NPC's and our PC's both physically and emotionally, and why we stop where we do, and in facts asks us if we're honest with our own reasons. It's a chance to realize terrible things about ourselves, and thus gives us a real chance to grow and develop. I like them for some of the same reasons I like Beast.<br /> <br /> Which, as a guy who pushes RPG's as art, art as communication, and communication as a spark for improvement, is a big deal.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I also like how, despite everything, they are among the most likely groups to treat monsters as people, rather than just prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-10-2018, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T22:08:45-08:00","id":791332,"title":"","content":"So... I'm starting to think that we are just arguing about semantics (yay Internet!) and in general all agree with each other. The sexual aspect of the Abbey needs to be toned down if it is to remain a PC option, in particular the way it handles rape. Instead of being tolerated/encouraged either actively or passively, it should be condoned, as this does not add significantly to the portrayal of the compact, and for some people it brings additional emotional baggage which changes roleplaying from a positive experience to an extremely negative one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T22:26:32-08:00","id":791339,"title":"","content":"Well, I have quoted the relevant parts of the book, and I will allow the evidence to speak for itself. I've stated my points to the point of repetition, so I'm pretty sure I've made it clear where I and other people stand on the issue. What is left now is, of course, entirely up to the developers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T01:02:55-08:00","id":791416,"title":"","content":"I think that any write-up in the 2nd edition needn't get into the ugly details of the AA's sexual practices, but like ArcaneArts said, I do think they represent an important and ugly component of the Vigil, and that point is perfectly illustrated <i>without </i>the bits about sexual violence. <br /> <br /> Honestly, it's been really bugging me how I keep seeing people saying that they don't think the AA make sense in the context of Hunter, but they offer a pretty distinctive, honest and somewhat repulsive perspective on the Vigil that's totally unique from the other main orgs. I hope Monica goes with the 2nd option to maintain part of what makes them interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T01:34:16-08:00","id":791424,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with what you and ArcaneArts are saying as positive thematic role the Abbey has to play, is that it is inherently flawed from the get go: they're 1% elitist snobs taken to near-cartoonish Hellfire Club shenanigans.<br /> <br /> There's simply too much going on with them to really achieve them as a narrative foil due to their lack of ideology beyond thrill-seeking. They would be far better for challenging the justifications of other Hunters, and providing challenging role-playing to players, if they weren't wrapped up in the hedonistic aristocrat deal (even discarding the sexual squick). The fact that they're wrapped up in all sorts of cultural baggage that the vast majority of the world's population both can't really relate to, and actively resents for it, it's too easy to dismiss them.<br /> <br /> Though I find the use of the words, &quot;honest,&quot; and, &quot;pure,&quot; about them exceedingly off-putting.<br /> <br /> If I want a group of Hunters that challenge all those things, I need ones that can't be dismissed as rich white people solving rich white problems with money, influence, and power. All of that taints their ability to really be challenging in-narrative or as a player. I'd much rather have a Compact like Project Mayhem from <i>Fight Club</i> if I wanted to do this (which works even better with the GMC side of things really).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T01:36:55-08:00","id":791425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791106#post791106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As things stand now, I consider the Abbey a bit of a missed opportunity. While the other Hunter organizations have aspects that can cast them in both good and bad light, Ashwood Abbey's presentation doubled down on the negative. I think &quot;Compacts and Conspiracies&quot; made a step in the right direction, by showing their thrill seeking as not necessarily repugnant.<br /> <br /> There aren't many hunters who would be willing to actually socialize with the monsters or to spend the night in a haunted locale just for kicks. Trying to make friends with monsters opens up many possibilities plot-wise, which trying to kill them - doesn't. With a greater network to fund their activities, advise them on the consequences and stage an intervention should things go too far, these Hunters could accomplish successes and cause disasters unthinkable in other organisations. Each story shared with the whole of the Compact would warn the members what not to do, or more likely, how to do damage control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this happening a bit. The Abbey tends to run much akin to a Spring Court at times if take away the Changeling aspect and the oaths keeping Changelings at play.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T03:30:21-08:00","id":791462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791220#post791220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really isn't the place to have a conversation about the issues that come up in our play groups. Nor is it a place to talk about the politics of fiction, what it depicts and why.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Yes, it is. That's what a forum thread about open development is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791277#post791277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Unihar went, so does this aspect of the Abbey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sold.<br /> <br /> I think Ashwood Abbey can retain certain characteristics about it that we all know and love while still trimming off some of the fat. But whatever, <b>Hunter</b> isn't really my thing anymore and AA never appealed to me anyway, so I don't know what I'm doing in this thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T06:23:43-08:00","id":791530,"title":"","content":"Hey, I wanted to drop by and mention that I appreciate this discussion. I've been reading through your comments, and they are helping me to make a better, more informed decision about the way forward. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T06:57:48-08:00","id":791541,"title":"","content":"Does this mean we could be getting a Patrick Bateman-style slasher antagonist?<br /> <br /> It's a bit off topic, but I think it could be cool (especially given the presumed focus of the new edition) to see a signature slasher from each compact and covenant to demonstrate how the ideology of each group makes them prone to corruption. I'd kind of like to start a thread devoted to workshopping those ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T06:59:23-08:00","id":791543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791530#post791530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I wanted to drop by and mention that I appreciate this discussion. I've been reading through your comments, and they are helping me to make a better, more informed decision about the way forward. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for drawing us in to the development cycle! I'm really excited to see how this game evolves in the second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:07:34-08:00","id":791548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791541#post791541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean we could be getting a Patrick Bateman-style slasher antagonist?<br /> <br /> It's a bit off topic, but I think it could be cool (especially given the presumed focus of the new edition) to see a signature slasher from each compact and covenant to demonstrate how the ideology of each group makes them prone to corruption. I'd kind of like to start a thread devoted to workshopping those ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Ashwood, Huntclub, Bear Lodge, TF:V? Easy to imagine. Union? Not so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:15:52-08:00","id":791555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791548#post791548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Ashwood, Huntclub, Bear Lodge, TF:V? Easy to imagine. Union? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Union is that much off a stretch. A corrupt and relentlessly unstoppable murder cop, a psychotic former firefighter pyromaniac, a racist and xenophobic utility worker who has access to the building plans in his city and knows how to get into any building committed to ridding his city of all the &quot;filth&quot;, supernatural or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:20:11-08:00","id":791556,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I think Kevin Garvey from The Leftovers could be a great inspiration for a Union slasher: an officer with serious anger issues who's well intentioned but goes into dissociative states where he'll wake up and realize he's committed horrible acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:21:29-08:00","id":791558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791548#post791548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. Ashwood, Huntclub, Bear Lodge, TF:V? Easy to imagine. Union? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, The Union are not that hard to twist around. Highlight the xenophobia, Focus on scarcity of resources, and ignorance of the greater world in an effort for a band-aid solution for now.<br /> <br /> &quot;Killing for the Cause&quot; can easily be pushed into killing political targets which quickly morphs into &quot;Killing who can threaten friends and family&quot; which turns into &quot;killing everyone but friends and family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just have to be careful that you don't end up sounding like Fox News propaganda when writing such examples down though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:27:39-08:00","id":791564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791558#post791558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, The Union are not that hard to twist around. Highlight the xenophobia, Focus on scarcity of resources, and ignorance of the greater world in an effort for a band-aid solution for now.<br /> <br /> &quot;Killing for the Cause&quot; can easily be pushed into killing political targets which quickly morphs into &quot;Killing who can threaten friends and family&quot; which turns into &quot;killing everyone but friends and family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just have to be careful that you don't end up sounding like Fox News propaganda when writing such examples down though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't emphasized in the original edition but, perhaps especially being from Atlanta, the term &quot;neighborhood guardians&quot; makes me think of hate groups and supremacy organizations.<br /> <br /> &quot;We don't hate anyone. We're just protecting our own,&quot; is a common rallying cry of bigots. That new neighbor? No. We aren't eyeing him up and down because he's brown and wears a funny beard. We just don't know what parasites might be following in his wake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 12-23-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:37:26-08:00","id":791570,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Cheiron had Bateman as a core sample hunter. The term Bateman then cropped up in Slashers as Cheiron code for an operative turned Slasher or Slasher operative. <br /> <br /> Slashers had samples for all the Compacts and Conspiracies falling, and a paticularly great Union one in the guy who viewed the Vigil as contagion and the site they used as the vector, basically hunting down his fellows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:37:26-08:00","id":791571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791564#post791564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't emphasized in the original edition but, perhaps especially being from Atlanta, the term &quot;neighborhood guardians&quot; makes me think of hate groups and supremacy organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at the history of early unions, you'll see many examples of the labor movement being divided on the issue until finally coming around to it.<br /> <br /> That being said, using them as a hate group foil is extremely disingenuous given that unions often took part in the civil rights movement.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:40:47-08:00","id":791577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791570#post791570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Cheiron had Bateman as a core sample hunter. The term Bateman then cropped up in Slashers as Cheiron code for an operative turned Slasher or Slasher operative. <br /> <br /> Slashers had samples for all the Compacts and Conspiracies falling, and a paticularly great Union one in the guy who viewed the Vigil as contagion and the site they used as the vector, basically hunting down his fellows</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? That sounds awesome. I borrowed a copy of Slashers but haven't had a chance to dig in. I look forward to flipping through it over the holiday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T07:42:47-08:00","id":791581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791571#post791571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you look at the history of early unions, you'll see many examples of the labor movement being divided on the issue until finally coming around to it.<br /> <br /> That being said, using them as a hate group foil is extremely disingenuous given that unions often took part in the civil rights movement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is if we assume they're a pure metaphor for traditional unions, but I'm not sure they are. I'm not suggesting the organization as a whole be presented as racist or xenophobic. I'm simply talking about the outliers... and as a group without a major leadership infrastructure, there's plenty of outliers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T08:39:46-08:00","id":791610,"title":"","content":"So it seems this discussion is now focused on the sexual violence aspect of the Abbey. So my views:<br /> <br /> I don't think the Abbey has institutionalised sexual violence. Quite the opposite actually, the Abbey's membership is mostly uncomfortable with sexual violence but being the worst sort of libertines their institutional culture also prevents them from expressing that disapproval.<br /> <br /> I think the section beginning &quot;Make no mistake&quot; - oft quoted to support the idea that the Abbey institutionalise sexual violence is actually saying the opposite and agrees with the above. When the narrator says &quot;It\u2019s not about sex&quot; what the narrator means is &quot;The Abbey is not about sexual violence&quot;. When the narrator follows that up with &quot;though it can be&quot; what the narrator means is &quot;but if it's your thing I won't object&quot;. Which is what I said in the preceding paragraph.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, whether the 1E Abbey has institutionalised sexual violence is not really that useful a discussion. The question is, should the 2E Abbey? And I think the answer is no. After all, the 1E Abbey didn't. I don't think you can say that the Abbey has an institutional policy of forbidding it's members from sexualised violence without breaking charachter, since &quot;no ethics&quot; is core to their charachter. But you can certainly take the spotlight away and give it to the Abbey members doing stuff like finding ways to fly or crashing Spring Court parties.<br /> <br /> Taking the spotlight away would probably require not mentioning sexualised violence even once. Even a single mention would most likely stick in the mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was also thinking a bit about how an Abbey Hunter could go from novelty seeking hedonist to a creature-of-habbit Slasher and I think I've identified two likely paths.<br /> 1) They find a kick they like so much they stop seeking novelty and seek more of the same. If there aren't enough monsters to supply their fix, they might turn to regular humans. E.G. An Abbey hunter who enjoys betraying others too much might run out of monsters, and become a Charmer.<br /> 2) The mortal world reminds the Abbey that they're not above the rules, and their rage overtakes their hedoism. E.G. A witch simply calls the police, an Abbey Hunter gets arrested, and breaks out to become an Avenger against every officer and lawyer who put him away.<br /> <br /> That said, I still think Claimed by Infernal Demons needs to be highlighted as a way Abbey hunters fall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791213#post791213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't trust the average roleplayer with a nuanced masterpiece of storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div> I oppose on principal any argument that begins with not trusting your audience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791213#post791213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds frighteningly like the &quot;racism has a place in the World of Darkness, because racism is dark!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Racism does have a place in the World of Darkness! Without racism I can't tell some of the stories that resonate with me. (I do this a more often than Hakollel. Look how often the theme of &quot;home is a special place&quot; crops up in my work).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791329#post791329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ashwood criticizes the justifications of Hunter flat out, and asks players to ask questions about play experiences: why do we enjoy a game about hunting monsters, tearing apart NPC's and our PC's both physically and emotionally, and why we stop where we do, and in facts asks us if we're honest with out own reasons. It's a chance to realize terrible things about ourselves, and thus gives us a real chance to grow and develop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you raise a very good point here. There's an awesome bit of meta to the Ashwood Abbey. The Abbey hunt monsters for fun, which is exactly the game we're all playing.<br /> <br /> I don't think we realize &quot;terrible things about ourselves&quot;, because unlike the Abbey we have a cast iron justification. We're only hurting fictional people, and we know why we do it. We're descended from aggressive apes with all sorts of bugs in the wetware, and thus we require an outlet and fiction has the immense advantage of not hurting real people.<br /> <br /> But still, the meta element is there and it's awesome. It would be a shame to loose it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-23-2015, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T09:00:51-08:00","id":791622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791610#post791610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can I put in a vote for Kings Raven to write for Hunter 2E?<br /> <br /> Oh, wait, I just did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T09:10:56-08:00","id":791626,"title":"","content":"This thread has gotten really long so forgive me if this has been brought up by a previous poster that I missed while skimming.<br /> <br /> Hunter as it is now has a bit of a problem with violence being treated as the norm in a way no other CofD game line has. It makes sense to a degree, after all the game is called Hunter not &quot;Aware Mortals&quot;. Still the basic goals of most compacts and conspiracies as they exist now is to capture or kill whatever supernaturals they find causing problems in whatever venue they focus on (with Network Zero being the main exception in the corebook). Even the non-violent sub-groups within the larger compacts are largely portrayed as support for violent field teams.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see more of an expansion on non-violent and less directly violent takes on the Vigil in the coming 2E.<br /> <br /> For Example:<br /> <br /> As it has been mentioned you can tone down or outright remove the sexual violence from Ashwood Abbey and reframe them as thrill seeking hedonists. Folks hunting down Mages to just to find out what various enchantments feel like, inviting themselves to Summer Court soirees to get a chance to taste goblin fruit or to have sex with a living ball of flame.<br /> <br /> TF:V could be framed as less genocidal towards monsters and more towards wanting to control them. Having intelligence agents act as liaisons to the entrenched supernatural organizations (Vampire Covens, Mage Orders, Werewolf Packs, etc) attempting to make arrangements with them to better serve the interests of the United States government (&quot;Drop some nasty magic on this remote village and we'll keep the other conspiracies off your back until we need you again), stepping in with the advanced hardware only when the monsters start to step out of line.<br /> <br /> The Union could tie more into the history of organized labor and civil rights movements. Putting more of an emphasis on community building with the Supernaturals to keep everyone safe (until other Hunters or rogue Supernaturals mess it up naturally). Rather than the rather nasty reactionary form they've taken in 1E that feels much more like one of those border guard militas than a union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T09:23:44-08:00","id":791633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791622#post791622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I put in a vote for Kings Raven to write for Hunter 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791626#post791626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter as it is now has a bit of a problem with violence being treated as the norm in a way no other CofD game line has.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh I definately agree with what you're saying and if I'm honest I kind of reached the point where I do consider the game to be &quot;Aware Mortals&quot;. I've written multiple non-violent orgs myself for fun.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't take away violence from the Abbey. Sometimes they just want to go fox hunting with a kitsune. But I would definately like to see more spotlighting non-violent activities. TF:V being more interested in control, sure.<br /> <br /> The Union though, nah. The Union are fine as they are, community building is kind of an Ascending One thing, kind of a Bijin thing. But mostly it's an unfilled niche that is ready for a new group to step in and do (unless you count fan groups. Then The Lord Stewards have it covered).<br /> <br /> <br /> On this subject I'd also definately like to see less of a belief that every group must make killing monsters a priority unless there a special exception. Take the Agis Kai Doru. I'd much rather they focused on the Relics and some grand plan when they aquire a set of legendary relics and only fight monsters if it furthered their goals; rather than Werewolf/Witch genocide being their actual goal.<br /> <br /> I'll stop here because this is off topic. But this topic will probably come up again later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T11:36:42-08:00","id":791707,"title":"","content":"Posted mine comment under dev blog, but here I will just sum up - <b>leave the Abbey more or less as it is</b>, only take the most disturbing sexual and torture aspects ( origin story with Reverend Ogilvy masturbating over werewolves corpses were too much a stretch <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Make Abbey most &quot;connected&quot; of Compacts - they can get you to the Supernatural parties and even some chapter houses go to late midnight dinners with Prince or branches with Ruling Council in Consilium. <i>Make Abbey as information and thrill brokers, that let other hunters to let some steam off, if they want to join them.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And make Hunt Club the Slashers mirror group that is &quot;scouting&quot; inside of Abbey. When the parties and &quot;those limits even Ashwood do not cross&quot; are not enough - there Hunt Club want you in.<br /> <br /> As general though - I all agree that there should be in each and every one of Compacts and Conspiracies examples of their memebers going into Slashers. In <i>Slashers Chronicles</i>, the most important aspect should be how easily the once Hunter can become Slasher and were the line is putted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T12:14:46-08:00","id":791734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791707#post791707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posted mine comment under dev blog, but here I will just sum up - <b>leave the Abbey more or less as it is</b>, only take the most disturbing sexual and torture aspects ( origin story with Reverend Ogilvy masturbating over werewolves corpses were too much a stretch <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Make Abbey most &quot;connected&quot; of Compacts - they can get you to the Supernatural parties and even some chapter houses go to late midnight dinners with Prince or branches with Ruling Council in Consilium. <i>Make Abbey as information and thrill brokers, that let other hunters to let some steam off, if they want to join them.</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And make Hunt Club the Slashers mirror group that is &quot;scouting&quot; inside of Abbey. When the parties and &quot;those limits even Ashwood do not cross&quot; are not enough - there Hunt Club want you in.<br /> <br /> As general though - I all agree that there should be in each and every one of Compacts and Conspiracies examples of their memebers going into Slashers. In <i>Slashers Chronicles</i>, the most important aspect should be how easily the once Hunter can become Slasher and were the line is putted.</div> </div> </div> </div>In his defence, he only masturbated over the standing stones so he could piss off the werewolves enough that they'd present themselves for his elephant gun. It was their origin that sort of made me fall in love with them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T13:26:10-08:00","id":791764,"title":"","content":"I like the Abbey more as a horrible mirror to the Vigil (&quot;Are we really like these sick bastards?&quot;) than as a playable group, and think they're much more effective thematically as such. Running up against the madmen who do kill for fun and sport makes you ask questions much more readily than playing them yourselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T14:01:53-08:00","id":791783,"title":"","content":"Of course, they also allow for their own swerve characters: The Abbey Hunter that actually behaves more morally than the other cell members just because they choose to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T17:02:12-08:00","id":791857,"title":"","content":"But that gets back into something brought up earlier:<br /> <br /> How &quot;more moral&quot; are they really being if they continue to belong to an organization that allows such depraved individuals to thrive? Abbey members don't just punch a membership card. They're expected to pay extremely high dues in an explicit pyramid scheme, funding whatever those above them get into.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not a murderer, but I give $50K to a group of people I know are sadistic thrill-killers,&quot; isn't exactly a highly moral stance.<br /> <br /> Playing a &quot;defector from decadence&quot; character that's no longer a member of the Abbey is one thing, but only heightens the nature of the Abbey as antagonists; since they tend to get fairly nasty with people that try to leave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T19:33:46-08:00","id":791918,"title":"","content":"Cross posted on the dev blog.<br /> <br /> Were I to make a choice between the presented options I would go with the second. My reasoning is as follows.<br /> First, I honestly like Ashwood Abbey (with a bit of a caveat that I will come back to in a moment). To me they have the ability to fill a number of niches in a Hunter story. Their adrenaline junkie approach to the Vigil as a sort of extreme sport creates the potential for novel or non-standard plot structures. To them the Vigil is excitement and adventure, asserting your humanity versus the monsters in the dark by living on the bleeding edge of your own limits. They also dovetail well with genre conventions of mysterious and decadent secret societies devoted to occult misadventures. Need one for your game? The Abbey will do just nicely.<br /> <br /> Now to address one of bigger sticking points. In their initial presentation the Abbey is alluded to sometimes engage in sexual congress with the denizens of the hidden world. So far so keeping with their theme, even if its an aspect I've never really used or seen other people explore. Once we get to their write-up in Compacts &amp; Conspiracies though things get a bit darker. Sexual violence becomes more explicitly part of their forte, and I think it contributes a lot to their squicky reputation among players. I know personally I don't really include that in \u201cmy\u201d chronicle of darkness, and though some might disagree I feel that excising or downplaying that would benefit the game without really losing much.<br /> <br /> I feel that blending Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club would be a good move on multiple levels. For one, it would acknowledge the fact that both compacts share a lot of thematic space in an in-universe way. They are literally in competition with each other. I feel that it would also create good story opportunities for the Abbey by forcing them into clarifying and justifying their own existence. They are trapped between a club of homicidal lunatics that includes a disturbing number of their former friends and other hunters who more often than not can't tell the two of them apart. If you're still in the Abbey, if you haven't jumped ship for the Hunt Club, why is that? It isn't enough just to be jaded and debauched anymore. There's a new kid on the block who will do all the things you won't. If it isn't just about the sex, drugs, and death then what 'is' it about?<br /> <br /> What is your Vigil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T20:25:26-08:00","id":791938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791764#post791764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Abbey more as a horrible mirror to the Vigil (&quot;Are we really like these sick bastards?&quot;) than as a playable group, and think they're much more effective thematically as such. Running up against the madmen who do kill for fun and sport makes you ask questions much more readily than playing them yourselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are <b><i>not</i></b> madman! They are bored, they are thrill-seekers - but not madman. Or not much more than rest of hunters. Let's look on other Tier 2 groups you compare those &quot;madman&quot; of yours. The rest of corebook hunters of this level are:<ul><li><b>Long Night</b> - Apocalypse cult freaks that many times are more bloody than the Inqusition itself</li> <li><b>Loyalist of Thule</b> - Guilt ridden occultists that are known from using blackmail, torture and other literal Nazis methods as are they their predescesors. Oh, did I forget that they are controlled by immoral mage-kings of probable Atlantis?</li> <li><b>Network Zero</b> - Crazy youtubers that want to film everything and show to world everything - even if those would put others in jeopardy and risk.</li> <li><b>Null Mysteriis</b> - scientific obsessed butchers that want to cut and experiment for months on inteligent, living beings ( &quot;monsters&quot; ) only to <i>know </i>things.</li> <li><b>The Union</b> - coalition of working class neighborhood watchers that maybe do the good work - only if they do not kill one another or open war with whole supernatural community of the city just because &quot;Johnny had bad day&quot;.</li> </ul>And you clearly say that thrill-seeking group here do not work? That they are worse than Night, Thule or Null? I openly stated that there are parts of 1ED Ashwood Abbey write-up that should be downplayed, but throwing them away is throwing the baby out with the bathwater.<br /> <br /> Also, from what I understand ( or hope at least ) is that <i>Slasher Chronicles</i> highlight how Hunters can easily become Slashers. Yours &quot;madmen who do kill for fun and sport&quot; are much more in the Slashers category - they can stem from Abbey, just as Apocalypse death cultists can originate from Long Night, modern Nazis can spring from Thule or scientific butchers can originate from Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br /> If you want to, you can call this psycho Slashers from Abbey as Hunt Club. But then you need to have nice names for others Compacts and Conspiracies Slashers groups - as Abbey is <b>not most decadent </b>to have Slashers hailing <b>only</b> from it. <b>All</b> Hunters Organistations generate Slashers. ( Or at least should be if we want to highlight name <i>Slashers Chronicles</i> ). This is exactly to &quot;makes you ask questions much more readily&quot; you asked for.<br /> <br /> <b><i>&quot;Everyone of us can become Slasher - if we do not take care of how we hunt. Or we start to pick who we hunt... &quot;</i></b><br /> <i>Mentor hunter to the new member</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-23-2015, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T06:21:16-08:00","id":792126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=791857#post791857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that gets back into something brought up earlier:<br /> <br /> How &quot;more moral&quot; are they really being if they continue to belong to an organization that allows such depraved individuals to thrive? Abbey members don't just punch a membership card. They're expected to pay extremely high dues in an explicit pyramid scheme, funding whatever those above them get into.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not a murderer, but I give $50K to a group of people I know are sadistic thrill-killers,&quot; isn't exactly a highly moral stance.<br /> <br /> Playing a &quot;defector from decadence&quot; character that's no longer a member of the Abbey is one thing, but only heightens the nature of the Abbey as antagonists; since they tend to get fairly nasty with people that try to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the response can be summed up with a distasteful &quot;to each their own&quot;. One is responsible for one's own actions. And a &quot;membership boycott&quot; isn't really going to accomplish anything without communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:17:51-08:00","id":792263,"title":"","content":"This is a duplicate of the comment that I made on the origin announcement:<br /> <br /> I have always liked the Ashwood Abbey, and I use them frequently. Although they frequently end up as antagonists in my games, the same is also true of many of the more religious organizations, and I don't want to see any of them placed into the &quot;Antagonists&quot; section by default. I think that the motivation of &quot;hunting for experiences&quot; is perfect for a hunter organization, and that a Hellfire Club is ideal for that role. Ultimately, the Abbey does need a bit of an update, but I don't think that said update needs to be in the form of changing which side they're on. The Abbey hunter that bankrolls the Vigil for a cell in exchange for getting to come along (or at least getting some of that vampire blood to bring to his next party) seems very appropriate to a hunter game. If they were to become default antagonists, that doesn't seem likely. It's a rare character that is willing to side with a known enemy, but siding with a questionable ally against a greater threat is a different story. There's a huge difference between &quot;That guy's one of the ones we need to take down,&quot; and &quot;That guy's an entitled asshole that we don't like, but he's still technically one of us.&quot; <br /> <br /> I think that any kind of update for the Abbey should focus a bit more heavily on the sheer variety of ways that they hunt. The Compacts and Conspiracies book depicted groups of the Abbey that weren't in it for the rape or the kill, and I think that a bit more space dedicated to hunters like that might help to ease a bit of the distaste people feel for them. Show the Abbey in a potentially more sympathetic light by portraying what some of the better ones are like, rather than focusing mostly on the sickest bastards of the bunch. I'm not saying that the worst that the Abbey can do should be left out entirely, but it should be established that it is the Abbey at its worst, and that not every Abbey hunter would go along with such behavior. In fact, I think that every hunter organization should show them at both their best and their worst.<br /> <br /> I also think that the Abbey could have the potential to be moved up to a third tier conspiracy with little effort. In Compacts and Conspiracies, it gave them the Bacchanal Endowment. I had been amused by that, as I'd given them an Endowment by the same name in the games I was using them in, and I think that there is a lot of potential for an Endowment based on ecstatic revelry. What if the Bacchanal Endowment actually had a bit more magical power behind it, rather than merely increasing their privilege and influence with various groups? It could grant them special Conditions, each with its own benefit and drawback, which could aid them in the hunt.<br /> <br /> I've noticed a lot of the others seem to want them to be treated as antagonists, and although I disagree, I'd like to make one request. Please don't make the perception of them as the antagonists a universal thing for the other organizations. Let the Abbey think of themselves as hunters like the other groups, and let the other groups think of them as hunters that have gone off the deep end. Let them be the dark side of &quot;us&quot; instead of just another group of &quot;them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:53:17-08:00","id":792478,"title":"","content":"I tend to use the Abbey in my games. I like them. Even when I'm not playing them, they serve a very good &quot;enemy of my enemy&quot; role that's not inherently antagonistic. <br /> <br /> That said, I personally feel that taking any human group and drawing a hard &quot;protagonist/antagonist&quot; line between them waters down what I feel Hunter is about. I'm actually kind of uncomfortable with Slashers for a handful of reasons. But I think they're about as far as I think Vigil should take drawing hard lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:33:19-08:00","id":792492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=792478#post792478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to use the Abbey in my games. I like them. Even when I'm not playing them, they serve a very good &quot;enemy of my enemy&quot; role that's not inherently antagonistic.<br /> <br /> That said, I personally feel that taking any human group and drawing a hard &quot;protagonist/antagonist&quot; line between them waters down what I feel Hunter is about. I'm actually kind of uncomfortable with Slashers for a handful of reasons. But I think they're about as far as I think Vigil should take drawing hard lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of the gamelines are really about good guys or bad guys, but Vigil's question of &quot;what monstrosity is worth hunting&quot; very particularly means that there can't be easy lines.<br /> <br /> If anything, more hunter organizations should leave you feel uneasy, rather than less.<br /> <br /> As a random note, I feel about The Union the way most people feel about the Ashwood Abbey. At least the Abbey admits something's a little screwed with their hedonism. The Union's xenophobia scares the crap out of me in a way the Abbey wishes they could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T19:47:11-08:00","id":792499,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with white oak dragon. C &amp; C really made the Abby less automatically antagonistic and drawing from that in the 2e core would be wonderful. I like the idea of playing an older female Abby character (maybe a wealthy romance author) who likes to play mischievous matchmaker with with the local supernaturals, setting them up with each other in ways that throw their alliances into chaos and send the city into a giant Romeo and Juliet reenactment (and then some changeling who thinks he's Puck gets involved sets things in am ore midsummer night's dream direction).<br /> <br /> But I think we all agree that the Abby needs to be retooled to be less about murder-fucking and more about messing with the supernatural socially and straight up hedonism. And whoever mentioned making a witch give you the ability to fly, that is what I imagine a lot of Abby types would do, since rape and torture just miss so much of what a rich person would do with the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 12-24-2015, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T20:42:58-08:00","id":792518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=792499#post792499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>But I think we all agree </u>that the Abby needs to be retooled to be less about murder-fucking and more about messing with the supernatural socially and straight up hedonism. And whoever mentioned making a witch give you the ability to fly, that is what I imagine a lot of Abby types would do, since rape and torture just miss so much of what a rich person would do with the supernatural.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>No, we don't &quot;all agree,&quot; because not all of &quot;us&quot; see AA for what others see them as. I never thought they were simply about &quot;murder fucking,&quot; and I don't have a problem with what little of it is there. If my ST uses it, cool. If they don't feel comfortable using it, then that's cool too. <br /> <br /> I don't see a problem with them as is, and I'd rather they not be changed, but I really wish people would stop speaking for me.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but this is like the third or fourth time I've seen someone say &quot;I think we all agree&quot; or some such, and well, that's not exactly true.<br /> <br /> To me, the AA is not broken. It doesn't need fixing. They are not about murder fucking. Murder fucking does not define them. And if that small aspect bothers you, then I wouldn't use it in the game. <br /> <br /> I think we can all...no. I won't do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:02:14-08:00","id":792527,"title":"","content":"I think the core problem is that each player and/or group has a distinct view on each group, coloured by first impressions, positive or negative experiences, and their own needs.<br /> <br /> For example, ArcaneArts brings up The Union as a terrifying group, which is the polar opposite of my own take on it, which was informed by my own positive first impression of them and my need to have a hunter group to root for and belong if I ever played the game, so I downplayed the negative aspects of The Union and emphasised their positive traits (like, say, I took the comment about the union not really caring about hunting the supernatural per se and going after whatever harms the neighborhood, so my Union instead of xenophobic is actually very supporting of the supernatural so long as it doesn't harm mortals).<br /> <br /> Obviously, the same is happening to the Ashwood Abbey. No matter what choice is made here, many people will dislike changes to a compact they like, many will dislike that they haven't been properly labeled as antagonists, and many will not care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:06:32-08:00","id":792532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=792518#post792518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, we don't &quot;all agree,&quot; because not all of &quot;us&quot; see AA for what others see them as. I never thought they were simply about &quot;murder fucking,&quot; and I don't have a problem with what little of it is there. If my ST uses it, cool. If they don't feel comfortable using it, then that's cool too.<br /> <br /> I don't see a problem with them as is, and I'd rather they not be changed, but I really wish people would stop speaking for me.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but this is like the third or fourth time I've seen someone say &quot;I think we all agree&quot; or some such, and well, that's not exactly true.<br /> <br /> To me, the AA is not broken. It doesn't need fixing. They are not about murder fucking. Murder fucking does not define them. And if that small aspect bothers you, then I wouldn't use it in the game.<br /> <br /> I think we can all...no. I won't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm Sorry. I agree that the AA isn't broken, I just think it needs to be clarified ( I guess retooled was the wrong word to use) that they aren't all about the murder fucking, since I think that wasn't so well communicated in the 1e before C &amp; C. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 12-25-2015, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:37:16-08:00","id":792545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=792532#post792532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm Sorry. I agree that the AA isn't broken, I just think it needs to be clarified ( I guess retooled was the wrong word to use) that they aren't all about the murder fucking, since I think that wasn't so well communicated in the 1e before C &amp; C. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all good. No harm done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T21:54:43-08:00","id":792556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=792499#post792499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with white oak dragon. C &amp; C really made the Abby less automatically antagonistic and drawing from that in the 2e core would be wonderful. I like the idea of playing an older female Abby character (maybe a wealthy romance author) who likes to play mischievous matchmaker with with the local supernaturals, setting them up with each other in ways that throw their alliances into chaos and send the city into a giant Romeo and Juliet reenactment (and then some changeling who thinks he's Puck gets involved sets things in am ore midsummer night's dream direction).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this view and idea - Ashwood Abbey should be a bit like mischevious Spring Court - they are about power, having fun and information. Even Spring Court sometimes mentioned sex and drugs, but most people do not see them that way, as initial write up stern from this - and that's what should be in 2ED Hunter. No need to be sex and torture in their new write up - just mark the hedonists and Liberitines, and rest of gameline community will say themeselves what there is under those stances. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Abbey should be hedonists, powerplayers and information brokers. The most deviant of them become Slashers and go to Hunt Club - with which Abbey <i>fiercely figh</i><i>t</i> for their reputation.<br /> <br /> I imagine now scene when Ashwood Abbey calls old &quot;fox hunting&quot; style mass chase after Hunt Club member that gone whole Slasher - what is better prey, than predator in the human flesh? Predator that also bring bad name to the Abbey itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-25-2015, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T00:30:50-08:00","id":793003,"title":"","content":"I think Option 3 would serve to broaden Hunter as a whole and rejuvenate Ashwood Abbey.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>In my play experience as a Storyteller the compact has been a source of conflict. One PC was an affluent S&amp;M enthusiast \u2013 he read the core and that\u2019s what sprung to mind for him. During one encounter with a \u2018black widow\u2019 (who happened to be an immortal Blood Bather) he was the only PC who bought into the monster\u2019s argument that her victims wanted to die. A later session involving the Little Black Book (WoD Reliquaries \u2013 a cursed item used to compel women into being raped) he manipulated another Hunter into letting him keep it, ostensibly to improve his prestige in the Abbey. In another game a player was Tommy Lansetta (from The Keepers SAS) an Ashwood mob brat. When the police became involved with a series of murders the cell was investigating the character had to \u2018go underground\u2019 as his mafia connections and appearance at crime scenes made him appear to be the culprit. Eventually the character lost his mind.<br /> <br /> The first example was genuine antagonism, the player leaned into the \u201cSomething has to be fucking something else.\u201d (to quote from Mortal Remains) of Ashwood Abbey and made a character that eventually betrayed his cell.</li> </ol>The second hit the \u201chumanity is fragile\u201d theme dead on. His reason for hunting (killing monsters for kicks and doing good incidentally) just wasn\u2019t enough for him to survive intact.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club are thematically drawn from the same well Hellfire Clubs and \u201cthe Most Dangerous Game\u201d. They are both firmly built on wealth, status, and hedonism. Ashwood even name checks \u201cThe Most Dangerous Game\u201d and the Hunt Club refers to its killing as the \u201cGreat Game\u201d. It\u2019s the same idea, they are hunting monsters for some kind of a sport, it\u2019s a game to them. The difference is Ashwood claims the prey are the villains, the Hunt Club knows that the hunters are.</li> </ol><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>It will make room for a new compact in Hunter, which as much as I love the game it lacks the \u2018global\u2019 reordering that Vampire 2<sup>nd</sup> and Werewolf 2<sup>nd</sup> have achieved.</li> </ol><br /> Consider this:<br /> <br /> <i>They began as Ashwood Abbey, now hunters have a new name for them \u201cthe hunt club.\u201d A fallen hunter compact born of all the misogyny, racisms, and classism of a 19<sup>th</sup> century aristocratic order who chose to hunt monsters simply for the thrill. Some new recruits and allies have no idea they\u2019re surrounded by killers and slashers until they find themselves standing over the corpse of a human being. There are rumors of a compact within the compact trying to reform Ashwood from within.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I think something along those lines would give Storytellers the latitude to not invalidate Ashwood Abbey characters that already exists, give hunters a dark and interesting set of antagonists, and create stories about the ones trying to save them or being drawn in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1783-spanishinquisition","name":"SpanishInquisition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T15:33:48-08:00","id":793292,"title":"","content":"Of the three options and how I interpreted them, I vote for 1 but with some modifications. I think the Abbey shouldn't be in the character creation chapter as an option as it stands, instead I think it should be mentioned in a <i>create your own </i>section for the Hunter axis as a failed or fallen compact/conspiracy. The section could explain the Abbey as we knew it in 1st Ed and then show the what happens when a group falls as it transitions from option 1 to option 2 and then collapses in on itself in a catastrophic self destruction before reaching option 3 because I'm certain they'd go out with a bang rather than become the Hunt Club outright. This would allow those of us who are fond of the Abbey keep them as we know them now in our hearts and mind, <i>which is to say ****ing on werewolf loci while being **** off by a faithful squire in the face of certain death which certainly involved unloading more than an elephant gun. </i><br /> <br /> My reasons for this are:<br /> 1) I love the abbey just the way they are but they are a group of Nihilist which requires just the right group/game to run smoothly making them more of resource book material.<br /> 2) I think Hunter could use a bit of history to liven it up some and why not a failed or fallen compact, in fact, add a few more so that the players understand the sacrifices that have to be made by any organization that has a firm foundation. Maybe even mention how hard it is to rally forces in the World of Darkness to show us why people have to do it behind closed doors in tier 3 games.<br /> 3) Because it'd make for a great story seed. The fallen compact/conspiracy will rise again. From the ancient Lodge in Scotland, the players could breathe life back in to the old girl until she was ready to make things bleed again, reforming it to something that the players would be proud to be a part of while it maintained a bit of the &quot;ultra-violence&quot; that we associate with it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:51:59-08:00","id":793367,"title":"","content":"On slashers, I'd like support for them as Solo operators who were never hunters, and maybe ideas for how they can serve as antaganists in other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T18:21:49-08:00","id":794520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=792492#post792492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the gamelines are really about good guys or bad guys, but Vigil's question of &amp;quot;what monstrosity is worth hunting&amp;quot; very particularly means that there can't be easy lines.<br /> <br /> If anything, more hunter organizations should leave you feel uneasy, rather than less.<br /> <br /> As a random note, I feel about The Union the way most people feel about the Ashwood Abbey. At least the Abbey admits something's a little screwed with their hedonism. The Union's xenophobia scares the crap out of me in a way the Abbey wishes they could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm down with you on this. This post, David's above, and The Kings Raven's prompted me to go back into every book and reread the sections on the Ashwood Abbey. I'm not quiet done, Mortal Remains is still left, but I think I'm getting direction on how I want to see the Abbey again. The Abbey of Spirit Slayers and Night Stalkers is much more in line with what I want to see. Rich, privileged thrill seekers who may be debaucherous, but they do it with class and decorum. They may be basterds, but they are magnificent, sophisticated basterds. <br /> <br /> Both Witch Finders and C&amp;C have these as themes too, but they also have some unfortunate lines in them. C&amp;C talks about the stereotype of Ashwood as &quot;monsters and rapists, [and that] for some that's certainly true.&quot; Witch Finders mostly conforms to my vision of Ashwood, but there's also a bit about cells that vote witches to be boring having such harmless things being done to them as &quot;dosing the witch's drink with Rohypnol and having some fun.&quot; This gets portrayed as a typical and harmless reaction, which is absolutely and wholely inappropriate. <br /> <br /> Other than that though, I'm firmly in camp 1 or 2 now, although I very much want to see a change in the Abbey coming down on anyone who even thinks of having sex without their partner's consent in the hardest way possible. Otherwise, a group of rich partygoers who are sophisticated as hell, and who are willing to give monsters a chance to justify their existence (especially if they are fun!)... That is compelling, and something that would be missed if Hunter went on without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:49:29-08:00","id":794605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794520#post794520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the Abbey coming down on anyone who even thinks of having sex without their partner's consent in the hardest way possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the issue, no? Any monsters that the Abbey has trapped or imprisoned, are free to do with what the Abbey pleases. That includes tying down a witch, or a werewolf, or a demon, and doing whatever disgusting, malicious, sexual, etc. thing to that creature. Again, this is part of what makes the Abbey the bad guys(if they choose to do this). They're not good people. And they're not supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Like the Cheiron Group. Like the Hunt Club, etc. Granted, the majority of Abbey are not rapists. Just like the majority of the Union are good people. But there are some bad eggs. And maybe the group looks the other way. Maybe it doesn't. <br /> <br /> Abbey is the Affluenza kid from Texas + college fraternity + sadistic and sexually perverted elitists all rolled into one. They're not good people. They're not supposed to be. <br /> <br /> And...I'm perfectly fine with that. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is Hunter the Vigil, which, by the blood soaked rage-written eyes of Chuck Wendig, was pretty damn close to perfect. And I'd rather not see anything with Abbey changed. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T21:55:30-08:00","id":794608,"title":"","content":"I think you're in the minority, and you will have to accept that some degree of change is coming towards the Ashwood Abbey, as it seems to be what the majority of the posters in this thread vaguely agree on. Just like I have to accept that it's not likely to be moved to the antagonist section (or, as it would be my preference, deleted entirely), you'll have to deal with the upcoming changes. Of course, finding the appropriate degree of change and the right direction to take it is going to be a challenge for the developers. I doubt they'll find a way to make everyone happy, so we'll just have to try and accept it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T22:06:51-08:00","id":794614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794605#post794605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's the issue, no? Any monsters that the Abbey has trapped or imprisoned, are free to do with what the Abbey pleases. That includes tying down a witch, or a werewolf, or a demon, and doing whatever disgusting, malicious, sexual, etc. thing to that creature. Again, this is part of what makes the Abbey the bad guys(if they choose to do this). They're not good people. And they're not supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Like the Cheiron Group. Like the Hunt Club, etc. Granted, the majority of Abbey are not rapists. Just like the majority of the Union are good people. But there are some bad eggs. And maybe the group looks the other way. Maybe it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Abbey is the Affluenza kid from Texas + college fraternity + sadistic and sexually perverted elitists all rolled into one. They're not good people. They're not supposed to be.<br /> <br /> And...I'm perfectly fine with that.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is Hunter the Vigil, which, by the blood soaked rage-written eyes of Chuck Wendig, was pretty damn close to perfect. And I'd rather not see anything with Abbey changed. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The point is for people to have fun with the game. Causing real world trauma in people is not fun. The number of people who have been imprisioned and tortured is much smaller than those that have been raped. If what you want is the Affluenza kids who think they can do whatever they want, I say that belongs in the antagonist section. Those are not protagonists I want in the games I play and would far rather have a different compact from some other part of the planet. It's also not an issue of not using them because it's about the message of the game. A message of &quot;some groups think sexual abuse is okay&quot; is not one I will support, even if it's a comically evil protaganist group, since some people still miss out on the fact it's not (which is not targeted at anyone here, just so we are clear. I am 100% certain that we can all make the distinction between what's real and what's not, as well as what's moral and what's not). The Abbey can be bad guys without being rapists. Even for a horror game, that's too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 12-29-2015, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T02:24:31-08:00","id":794702,"title":"","content":"Which again, rolls round to the problem of &quot;how do you reign in the outliers in an organisation that prides itself on excess and boundary pushing? Obviously steps have been made, like with the presentation in C&amp;C and others which try to moderate the tone, and even in the core where everyone else sort of looks askance and judges the Libertines. Personally I think that, especially with their harsh punishments for people who resort to hunting humans, that the shadow war with the Hunt Club would allow for those proscriptions to set in, and for the Abbey to start to be a lot more pro-active in setting boundaries and trying to claw back their reputation.<br /> <br /> Like SecondChance put it, &quot;magnificent sophisticated bastards&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, how much &quot;bite&quot; the Abbey has is up to individual players and storytellers. The important thing is that if someone is going to use or play to the rape angle, then they see that their actions have consequences- be it from the organisation, their cell mates, or other avenues. Ultimately how much do we gain from outright omission?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:53:57-08:00","id":794826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794702#post794702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ultimately how much do we gain from outright omission?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO? The gains are all OOC. Onyx Path demonstrates sensitivity towards a large but sometimes invisible section of the audience. OPP continues to demonstrate its progressive values and its rejection of the misogyny that sadly runs deep in gaming culture. They already do a fantastic job of that and I am extraordinarily proud to support this company because of it. Hunter will also become more accessible to a wider range of people because, for better or worse, people in general are much, much more comfortable with physical violence than sexual violence. So I see dropping the rape angle as both a powerful statement and a way to grow the game.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, how much do lose in outright omission of sexual violence? Noting that I mean just omission here, not the condemnation that I've said I'd like to see... I don't think we losing anything at all. As has been pointed out, while the Abbey has a sexual side for sure, it's more focused on having a good time not on rape. They push the boundaries, but there are some they won't push right in the first chapter of the core book. They can be sophisticated evil bastards without being rapists. I honestly don't see what the benefits of hanging on to this would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T09:10:34-08:00","id":794883,"title":"","content":"I'm all for rejecting those sorts of values, of course, but I think that from a narrative point of view that sort of thing -needs- to be maintained even just as a reference. Because if you excise it totally, then what is really driving the Abbey that makes them more likely to jump ship to the Hunt Club or become slashers?<br /> <br /> You have to acknowledge the line, even if it's just in terms of it being &quot;The ones who go too far are the ones who turn&quot;. If you outright excise it, then there's nothing to push against if it does fall to option 2 and become a struggle of moralities (or levels of amorality). If we erase the Abbeys sins rather than qualifying them, then does that really help to overcome them?<br /> <br /> If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> Like surely it's better to make clear that the Abbey had a rape problem and took steps to remedy it, made examples and the like, than to simply vanish the problem and act like it was never a problem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 12-29-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T09:24:26-08:00","id":794892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794883#post794883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for rejecting those sorts of values, of course, but I think that from a narrative point of view that sort of thing -needs- to be maintained even just as a reference. Because if you excise it totally, then what is really driving the Abbey that makes them more likely to jump ship to the Hunt Club or become slashers?<br /> <br /> You have to acknowledge the line, even if it's just in terms of it being &amp;quot;The ones who go too far are the ones who turn&amp;quot;. If you outright excise it, then there's nothing to push against if it does fall to option 2 and become a struggle of moralities (or levels of amorality). If we erase the Abbeys sins rather than qualifying them, then does that really help to overcome them?<br /> <br /> If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> Like surely it's better to make clear that the Abbey had a rape problem and took steps to remedy it, made examples and the like, than to simply vanish the problem and act like it was never a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>That I agree with 100%. In fact, that's really what I would like to see since it maintains continuity and shows growth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:33:29-08:00","id":794928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794883#post794883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like surely it's better to make clear that the Abbey had a rape problem and took steps to remedy it, made examples and the like, than to simply vanish the problem and act like it was never a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think something like this will introduce a contradiction to the Abby's core charachter. The Abbey are about violating rules, giving them any rules other than &quot;don't spoil other member's fun&quot; just doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Which is one of the two reasons why I prefer outright omission, the other being that sex tends to overshadow other aspects of people's charachter. Witness how people's impressions of 1E Abbey tended towards &quot;every hunt ends 'then I stick my dick in it'&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides I don't think the Abbey needs morality to explain why they're not the Hunt Club. The Abbey are about violating rules, the Club are a traditonalst rule bound organisation. As for Slashers, while injecting Goblin drugs and having orgies with the spring court might break way more of societies rules than staking a vampire; it doesn't seem particularly likely to make serial killers - well I suppose it depends just what's in those Goblin drugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:44:09-08:00","id":794986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794928#post794928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides I don't think the Abbey needs morality to explain why they're not the Hunt Club. The Abbey are about violating rules, the Club are a traditonalst rule bound organisation. As for Slashers, while injecting Goblin drugs and having orgies with the spring court might break way more of societies rules than staking a vampire; it doesn't seem particularly likely to make serial killers - well I suppose it depends just what's in those Goblin drugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all fun and games until someone eats the Murderfruit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T12:20:40-08:00","id":795009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794928#post794928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think something like this will introduce a contradiction to the Abby's core charachter. The Abbey are about violating rules, giving them any rules other than &quot;don't spoil other member's fun&quot; just doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enh, I dunno if I can buy this characterization. Let me sort of step through it.<br /> <br /> The Abbey kills monsters for being <i>boorish company</i>, they're hardly <i>nonjudgmental</i>. High society excess has tons of (sometimes unspoken) rules that People of Class are expected to Just Know, whether it be about the etiquette of bringing your mistress to a social function or which cut of jacket to wear on a quasi-legal foxhunt. Even inside the Abbey there will be an intuitive layer of codes of conduct, an ability to read the atmosphere, that lets an Abbey hunter know that using a golf club to hit a wounded witch in the ribs a <i>fourth </i>time is absolutely <i>hilarious </i>while a <i>fifth </i>hit is obviously crass (&quot;Taking it all too a bit too <i>seriously</i>, good man.&quot;) and will see him uninvited from all of the season's important social functions.<br /> <br /> The Abbey's doormen would turn away someone attempting to attend the hunt in a t-shirt and jeans<i>, </i>because, really, One Simply Doesn't, do they? Being transgressive in certain avenues doesn't mean that they don't hold to a whole constellation of implicit and explicit rules rigorously. Let's put it this way: Who has more (official and unofficial) rules about dress, membership, and conduct, a street gang or a country club? Which one is a hunter from the Abbey more likely to be a member of?<br /> <br /> The Hunt Club's scoring system, traditions, and rotation of judges aren't going to be at all alien to members of the Abbey - they're familiar trappings that mirror the ways in which the Abbey's hunts are social events (often with their own traditions and rules, like drawing lots or jockeying for points.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T12:33:13-08:00","id":795015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795009#post795009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enh, I dunno if I can buy this characterization. Let me sort of step through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> The Abbey's transgression of cultural norms and &quot;everyone is a valid target and you can do whatever you want to them&quot; motto is not the same as &quot;you can do whatever you want, period.&quot; The Abbey is a counter-culture. It still has mores that define its own subculture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T12:37:39-08:00","id":795017,"title":"","content":"I think you're making a simple mistake about the fundamental core of the Abbey.<br /> <br /> The Abbey are not a Compact of the upper class. They're a hellfire club, that's the place where upper class ladies and gentlemen go to escape the stifling rules that surround the rest of their lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hunter Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He held debauched court over one of the several so-called \u201cHellfi re Clubs\u201d: secret societies of like-minded, well-connected men and women who sought to smash the taboos of the day. By modern standards, the recreational drugs, casual sex and public bondage-play were pretty tame. Rev. Ogilvy, a thinker ahead of his time, seemed to understand that. He urged his followers to break the rules any way they could.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously they'll have some rules, but I imagine all of them will just be codifications of one of two principals &quot;Don't ruin my fun&quot; and &quot;Don't endanger other members&quot;.<br /> <br /> So take your example of turning up in jeans and a t-shirt. That could be construed as 'runing my fun' - &quot;The theme of this evening's Kitsune hunt, is classic English fox hunting&quot;. But at the same time, I could just as easily see the Abbey saying &quot;I have invited a mad scientist with virtual reality helmets and the most elaborate pornography. The dress code shall be jeans and those delightfully droll t-shirts that's all the range with programmers these days.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:11:49-08:00","id":795039,"title":"","content":"Isn't that rather immaterial?<br /> <br /> The fact that it's okay to get sloppily drunk at an Abbey function (and not at a Society Dinner) doesn't mean you are free to get <i>classlessly </i>drunk at an Abbey function and violate the compact's codes, whether those codes are enumerated or not. If the Abbey was actually about smashing down barriers, they wouldn't have such a selective membership; but even when you're up to your eyeballs in supernatural cocaine One Doesn't Rub Elbows With The Help<i>, </i>except as a short-term divertissement or as part of a cruel joke. You could write several rather substantial essays on all the understood rules of marital infidelity in upper-class culture, even as it was pursued by the &quot;libertine&quot; set - even if you're violating your society's laws and taboos, you haven't actually set aside the expected dignities of your social class.<br /> <br /> The fact that you posit that it's okay to show up in casual wear <i>if the host</i> <i><b>mandates</b> that you ought to </i>is rather a case <i>for </i>the existence of rules, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T13:39:41-08:00","id":795051,"title":"","content":"That's not what I said. I said a large part of the appeal of hellfire clubs like the Abbey is that it <i>is</i> the one place a gentleman or lady is free to get classlessly drunk. (I don't think many do, but I think they like the fact they can, and the stuff they are doing would be even more scandulous than getting classlessly drunk)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795039#post795039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One Doesn't Rub Elbows With The Help<i>, </i>except as a short-term divertissement or as part of a cruel joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't there something in the books where the once a year an Abbey club give a homeless bum a one night taste of the good life; with most dying at the end but a lucky few graduating to full membership.<br /> <br /> The Abbey don't just hire anyone, Compacts and Conspiracies makes it clear that they expect their rich members to do the scutwork. But at at the same time they do break down class barriers in their own way. Old Money, New Money, and rich young punks are all members. Bear in mind that only one of those three groups is the etiquette culture society you're describing in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795039#post795039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that you posit that it's okay to show up in casual wear <i>if the host</i> <i><b>mandates</b> that you ought to </i>is rather a case <i>for </i>the existence of rules, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the host is aloud to mandate things that would be utterly scandulous and Just Not Done in upper class society suggests that the Abbey's rulebook bears little resembence to the contry club society it's members are seeking a little escape from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-29-2015, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T14:41:56-08:00","id":795091,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if this is a tasteless idea or not, but maybe make it that the Abbey doesn't just see rape as wrong, but <i>boring</i>? Like, it's seen as the domain of dullards and try-hards laking actual imagination? Probably a stupid idea, but just my attempt to throw my hat into the ring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T16:53:51-08:00","id":795197,"title":"","content":"The problem with that is if one form of sexual violence has become boring, a significant portion of the Abbey are going to see that as a challenge to take it even farther to a new extreme rather than give up on it completely.<br /> <br /> I don't want to get too much into spoilers or triggers, but the 2003 movie <i>Oldboy</i> is kind of what I'd imagine an Abbey member bored with &quot;simple&quot; sexual violence on targets might come up with (though the motivations of the antagonist in the film is not what I'd attribute to an Abbey hunter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:38:45-08:00","id":795284,"title":"","content":"Right, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T20:56:02-08:00","id":795362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=794608#post794608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're in the <b>minority</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I don't agree with that, either. The voices screaming for option 3(or otherwise) may be a bit &quot;louder,&quot; but here and other social media sites seem to say otherwise. I've certainly seen as many, if not more people clamor for options 1 and/or 2.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T21:17:53-08:00","id":795369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795362#post795362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I don't agree with that, either. The voices screaming for option 3(or otherwise) may be a bit &amp;quot;louder,&amp;quot; but here and other social media sites seem to say otherwise. I've certainly seen as many, if not more people clamor for options 1 and/or 2.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Option 2 still involves Ashwood changing. It's the one that I'm most in favour of, and I want to see pretty significant changes. I've seen little to no support for leaving things exactly as they are, it's almost all been 2 or 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T23:49:49-08:00","id":795423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795362#post795362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I don't agree with that, either. The voices screaming for option 3(or otherwise) may be a bit &amp;quot;louder,&amp;quot; but here and other social media sites seem to say otherwise. I've certainly seen as many, if not more people clamor for options 1 and/or 2.<br /> <br /> Just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Option 2 is definitely the most popular at the moment and it involves changing the Abbey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T00:43:14-08:00","id":795458,"title":"","content":"Hopefully if option 2 takes place this long discussion would modify it. If Abbey members are becoming Slashers (I still think Claimed by Infernal Demons needs to be a big part of how Abbey hunters fall) they probably wouldn't be joining the Hunt Club but taking a different more libertine path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T02:28:59-08:00","id":795892,"title":"","content":"I think that if the Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club become the same Compact, it's not going to mean that the Abbey simply disappears and becomes the Hunt Club, but that they influence each other. Surely the Abbey will loosen up some (if not most) of the Hunt Club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T03:51:45-08:00","id":796763,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but I don't like thematic dilution. I'd rather the Abbey remain the Abbey and Club remain the Club rather than both become something that's neither fish nor foul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T03:55:35-08:00","id":796764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795892#post795892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that if the Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club become the same Compact, it's not going to mean that the Abbey simply disappears and becomes the Hunt Club, but that they influence each other. Surely the Abbey will loosen up some (if not most) of the Hunt Club.</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt it. Group think implies that like-minded groups that associate like that closely tend to become more extreme in their thoughts. If anything, it would drive both groups into full Slasher-hood themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T04:54:43-08:00","id":796780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795369#post795369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen little to no support for leaving things exactly as they are, it's almost all been 2 or 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. I see things quite differently from you, I guess. Just went over this thread and saw a number of people state that if they had to choose, they'd go for option 1. Looking at the blog post on the front page, there's also a number of people that voted no change. Looking at rpgnet forums, there are a number of people that said option 1.<br /> <br /> It simply appears to me that the ones that want option 3, want to continue to tell everyone about option 3(you, Atamajakki, ShadowKnight). Which is fine. But to say you've seen <b>&quot;little to no support&quot;</b> is a bit absurd. Either you're trolling, being a bit silly, or you're not looking hard enough.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying more people aren't voting for option 2, either. I'm simply saying it's easy to see that there are quite a few people that are voting for option 1 and no change to the Abbey, whether here or elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 12-30-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:38:50-08:00","id":797023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795458#post795458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully if option 2 takes place this long discussion would modify it. If Abbey members are becoming Slashers (I still think Claimed by Infernal Demons needs to be a big part of how Abbey hunters fall) they probably wouldn't be joining the Hunt Club but taking a different more libertine path.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please note that in the Slasher Chronicle any hunter, from any compact, has the potential to become a slasher. This includes the Abbey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T14:58:49-08:00","id":797030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mlvalentine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=797023#post797023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please note that in the Slasher Chronicle any hunter, from any compact, has the potential to become a slasher. This includes the Abbey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well of course.<br /> <br /> Chalk this one up to imprecise wording. When I said &quot;If Abbey members&quot; I meant &quot;if an Abbey members are becoming Slashers in large numbers then...&quot; not &quot;if it is possible for an Abbey Hunter to become a Slasher&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:18:28-08:00","id":797039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/790883-slashers-ashwood-abbey-open-dev?p=795458#post795458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully if option 2 takes place this long discussion would modify it. If Abbey members are becoming Slashers (I still think Claimed by Infernal Demons needs to be a big part of how Abbey hunters fall) they probably wouldn't be joining the Hunt Club but taking a different more libertine path.</div> </div> </div> </div> I picked option 2 because i'm looking for a group that comes together to blow off steam but has the potential to turn bad. I thinking potential &quot;Batman vs. Joker&quot; dichotomy that has the idea but not the actual people. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:"